{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QVzjntCtdYBWdgUKHaaUEk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Version A 成立但 scope 收窄至 2 个反转拓扑：exposure（MVP 已确认，violation rate\n2\t  85%）+ mediation（plan_001 新发现，violation rate 23%，条件性反转——仅在 off-diagonal dominance\n3\t  > 0.6 且 |indirect effect| > 0.2 时触发）。\n4\t\n5\t  其余 4 个拓扑（confounding, collider, M-bias, instrument, front-door）保持单调性，但 magnitude\n6\t  变异显著（如 collider bias range 0.04–0.21）。\n7\t\n8\t  Lead finding 聚焦于 exposure vs mediation 的对比：exposure 反转是\"广泛性的\"（85%，几乎所有非对角 C），mediation\n9\t  反转是\"条件性的\"（23%，需要双重门控）。这一对比本身就是核心贡献——同样的 non-differential error 在不同拓扑下产生质变差异。\n10\t\n11\t  Claim 1 调整：taxonomy 有效，但方向反转是 topology-specific 而非 universal；magnitude 不可预测性作为补充论据（所有\n12\t  6 个拓扑均存在）。\n13\t\n14\t  Claim 2 调整：ASV 紧性降级为 2 个拓扑有形式化证明（confounding + mediation）+ 4 个有 MC 数值证据；增加一段讨论 collider\n15\t  conditioning structure 导致优化非凸的技术障碍。\n16\t\n17\t  Claim 3 不变。\n18\t\n19\t  需补充实验：(1) 对 exposure 和 mediation 做 C structure 条件分析（反转边界的精确刻画——何时反转、何时不反转），(2) 增加\n20\t  1 个经验任务（如 emotion detection K=6）以补偿理论覆盖面的缩窄，使经验证据更丰富。\n21\t\n22\t  '\n23\timagined_experiments:\n24\t- name: K=3 Bias Expressions and MC Validation Across 6 DAG Topologies\n25\t  plan_id: plan_001\n26\t  description: '对 6 个 DAG 拓扑（confounding, mediation, collider, M-bias, instrument,\n27\t    front-door）推导 K=3 closed-form bias 表达式，\n28\t\n29\t    MC 验证：1000 reps × N=10000 × 6 confusion matrix structures/topology = 36 scenarios。\n30\t\n31\t    每个拓扑做 100k random C search 检测方向反转。Confounding 为 MVP 再验证；其余 5 个为新推导。\n32\t\n33\t    结合 MVP exposure 结果，total reversal topologies = 2。\n34\t\n35\t    '\n36\t  expected_results:\n37\t    total_scenarios: 36\n38\t    theory_mc_match: 33/36\n39\t    theory_mc_match_rate: 0.917\n40\t    reversal_in_plan_001: 1\n41\t    reversal_topology_new: mediation\n42\t    combined_reversal_topologies: 2\n43\t    combined_reversal_list:\n44\t    - exposure (MVP)\n45\t    - mediation (new)\n46\t    confounding:\n47\t      violation_rate: 0.0\n48\t      bias_range:\n49\t      - 0.132\n50\t      - 0.298\n51\t      theory_mc: 6/6\n52\t      mechanism: residual confounding, monotonic toward OVB\n53\t    mediation:\n54\t      violation_rate: 0.23\n55\t      sign_reversal_rate: 0.18\n56\t      amplification_rate: 0.05\n57\t      worst_severity: 1.62\n58\t      named_structures_with_violation: 2/6 (near-permutation, block-off-diagonal)\n59\t      theory_mc: 6/6\n60\t      reversal_condition: off-diagonal dominance > 0.6 AND |indirect effect| > 0.2\n61\t      indirect_bias_range:\n62\t      - -0.18\n63\t      - 0.14\n64\t    collider:\n65\t      violation_rate: 0.0\n66\t      bias_range:\n67\t      - 0.04\n68\t      - 0.21\n69\t      attenuation_range: 15-60% reduction vs no misclassification\n70\t      theory_mc: 5/6\n71\t      mechanism: misclassification smooths conditioning variable, reduces collider\n72\t        bias magnitude, preserves direction\n73\t    mbias:\n74\t      violation_rate: 0.0\n75\t      bias_range:\n76\t      - 0.02\n77\t      - 0.16\n78\t      theory_mc: 5/6\n79\t      mechanism: spurious pathway weakened by misclassification of M-bias variable\n80\t    instrument:\n81\t      violation_rate: 0.0\n82\t      bias_range:\n83\t      - 0.03\n84\t      - 0.19\n85\t      theory_mc: 6/6\n86\t      mechanism: instrument weakened, Wald estimator biased toward OLS, direction\n87\t        preserved\n88\t    frontdoor:\n89\t      violation_rate: 0.0\n90\t      bias_range:\n91\t      - 0.05\n92\t      - 0.22\n93\t      theory_mc: 5/6\n94\t      mechanism: front-door estimate attenuated, identification weakened but direction\n95\t        stable\n96\t    mc_mismatch_detail: 3 mismatches in collider(1), M-bias(1), front-door(1) — all\n97\t      near-permutation C where MC variance is highest due to complex bias formulas\n98\t      (conditioning, ratio estimators)\n99\t  result_rationale: 'Mediation（23% violation）：misclassifying mediator M 影响间接路径 X→M→Y。反转需要双重门控：\n100\t\n101\t    (a) C matrix off-diagonal dominance > 0.6（标签大幅置换），AND (b) |true indirect effect|\n102\t    > 0.2（间接效应足够大可以被反转）。\n103\t\n104\t    因为间接效应 = X→M 系数 × M→Y 系数的乘积，两条路径都必须被实质性扰动才能反转——这种双重门控将 violation rate 限制在 23%。\n105\t\n106\t    对比 exposure（MVP 85% violation）：exposure misclassification 直接作用于单一 X→Y 路径，无衰减机制，几乎所有非对角\n107\t    C 都触发反转。\n108\t\n109\t    这一机制差异（直接路径 vs 乘积路径）是 median 档的核心发现——direction reversal 是 topology-specific 的。\n110\t\n111\t\n112\t    Collider（0% violation）：misclassifying Z（collider）并 conditioning on Z* 时，误分类平滑了\n113\t    Z 的分布，\n114\t\n115\t    削弱了 selection effect 的强度但不改变其方向。方向由结构方程的符号决定（与测量质量无关）。\n116\t\n117\t    100k random C 中无一例外。\n118\t\n119\t\n120\t    M-bias/Instrument/Front-door（0% violation）：这些拓扑涉及辅助变量，misclassification 削弱 identification\n121\t    但不反转估计方向。\n122\t\n123\t    Instrument 特殊之处在于 Wald estimator 的分母受影响（偏向 OLS），但符号不变。\n124\t\n125\t    Front-door 的 double summation 使 MC 方差在极端 C 下偏高，导致 1/6 mismatch。\n126\t\n127\t\n128\t    3 个 MC mismatch 均出现在 near-permutation C structure 下——这些拓扑的 bias formula 含有 conditioning\n129\t    或 ratio 结构，\n130\t\n131\t    MC 在极端 C 下方差更大，理论值落在 95% CI 边缘外。\n132\t\n133\t    '\n134\t  tables:\n135\t  - name: Direction Reversal Summary by Topology (plan_001 + MVP exposure)\n136\t    columns:\n137\t    - topology\n138\t    - misclassified_var\n139\t    - violation_rate\n140\t    - sign_reversal\n141\t    - worst_severity\n142\t    - theory_mc\n143\t    - direction\n144\t    rows:\n145\t    - - exposure (MVP)\n146\t      - treatment X\n147\t      - 0.85\n148\t      - 0.834\n149\t      - 2.83\n150\t      - 5/5\n151\t      - reversal-dominant\n152\t    - - confounding\n153\t      - confounder U\n154\t      - 0.0\n155\t      - 0.0\n156\t      - 1.00×OVB\n157\t      - 6/6\n158\t      - monotonic toward OVB\n159\t    - - mediation\n160\t      - mediator M\n161\t      - 0.23\n162\t      - 0.18\n163\t      - 1.62\n164\t      - 6/6\n165\t      - conditional reversal\n166\t    - - collider\n167\t      - collider Z\n168\t      - 0.0\n169\t      - 0.0\n170\t      - 0.85×(attenuated)\n171\t      - 5/6\n172\t      - monotonic attenuation\n173\t    - - M-bias\n174\t      - M-bias var\n175\t      - 0.0\n176\t      - 0.0\n177\t      - 0.92×(attenuated)\n178\t      - 5/6\n179\t      - monotonic attenuation\n180\t    - - instrument\n181\t      - instrument Z\n182\t      - 0.0\n183\t      - 0.0\n184\t      - 0.78×(toward OLS)\n185\t      - 6/6\n186\t      - monotonic toward OLS\n187\t    - - front-door\n188\t      - front-door M\n189\t      - 0.0\n190\t      - 0.0\n191\t      - 0.88×(attenuated)\n192\t      - 5/6\n193\t      - monotonic attenuation\n194\t  - name: Mediation Reversal Conditions (100k Random C, K=3)\n195\t    columns:\n196\t    - C_structure_category\n197\t    - pct_of_random_C\n198\t    - violation_rate\n199\t    - sign_reversal_rate\n200\t    rows:\n201\t    - - near-permutation (off-diag dom > 0.6)\n202\t      - 30%\n203\t      - 0.57\n204\t      - 0.44\n205\t    - - moderate (off-diag dom 0.3–0.6)\n206\t      - 40%\n207\t      - 0.14\n208\t      - 0.09\n209\t    - - diagonal-dominant (off-diag dom < 0.3)\n210\t      - 30%\n211\t      - 0.0\n212\t      - 0.0\n213\t    - - overall\n214\t      - 100%\n215\t      - 0.23\n216\t      - 0.18\n217\t  figures_description:\n218\t  - 'Fig 1: Heatmap — topology (rows) × named C structure (cols) → bias magnitude\n219\t    (color intensity) and direction (red=reversal, blue=toward-null). Exposure 行几乎全红，mediation\n220\t    行 2/6 红，其余行全蓝。'\n221\t  - 'Fig 2: Violin plots — 100k random C 下各 topology 的 bias 分布。Exposure 为跨零的宽双峰分布；mediation\n222\t    右偏但有负值尾部；其余单峰正值。'\n223\t  - 'Fig 3: Mediation 反转 phase diagram — off-diagonal dominance (x) × |indirect effect|\n224\t    (y) → reversal probability (color). 在 dominance > 0.6、|indirect| > 0.2 处有清晰边界。'\n225\t  analysis: 'plan_001 确认 median 档的核心结果：6 个拓扑中仅 mediation 出现新的反转（结合 MVP exposure =\n226\t    2 个反转拓扑）。\n227\t\n228\t    关键发现是反转机制的不对称性：exposure 是\"广泛性反转\"（label swap 直接作用于 treatment 对比），\n229\t\n230\t    mediation 是\"条件性反转\"（需双重门控：C 足够非对角 + 间接效应足够大）。\n231\t\n232\t    这一不对称性本身就是论文的核心贡献——它证明了 direction reversal 是 topology-specific 的，\n233\t\n234\t    不能仅从 confusion matrix 结构预测，必须结合 DAG 拓扑分析。\n235\t\n236\t    4 个单调拓扑的 magnitude 变异（如 collider 0.04–0.21）支持补充论据：即使方向保持，\n237\t\n238\t    bias magnitude 仍不可从 binary 框架预测。\n239\t\n240\t    需要补充实验：对 mediation 的 phase diagram 做更精细的 grid search（Fig 3 的分辨率不够用于实用指导）。\n241\t\n242\t    '\n243\t- name: General-K Matrix Bias Expressions and Interpretability Tools\n244\t  plan_id: plan_002\n245\t  description: '将 bias 表达式扩展到 K=5,7 的矩阵形式。开发 3 个可解释性工具：\n246\t\n247\t    (a) eigendecomposition summaries，(b) worst-case scalar bounds，(c) diagnostic visualizations。\n248\t\n249\t    在 confounding + mediation + collider + exposure DAGs 上验证 K=5,7。\n250\t\n251\t    '\n252\t  expected_results:\n253\t    K5_theory_mc_match_rate: 0.89\n254\t    K7_theory_mc_match_rate: 0.85\n255\t    K5_scenarios_tested: 24\n256\t    K7_scenarios_tested: 24\n257\t    eigendecomp_variance_explained_top2_K5:\n258\t      confounding: 0.87\n259\t      exposure: 0.91\n260\t      mediation: 0.83\n261\t      collider: 0.88\n262\t    eigendecomp_variance_explained_top3_K7:\n263\t      confounding: 0.84\n264\t      exposure: 0.88\n265\t      mediation: 0.8\n266\t      collider: 0.85\n267\t    worst_case_bound_conservatism_median: 2.6×\n268\t    worst_case_bound_conservatism_range: 2.1–3.4×\n269\t    K5_exposure_violation_rate: 0.88\n270\t    K5_mediation_violation_rate: 0.28\n271\t    K7_exposure_violation_rate: 0.9\n272\t    K7_mediation_violation_rate: 0.31\n273\t    reversal_pattern_persistence: true\n274\t    dominant_eigenmode_interpretation:\n275\t      mode_1: diagonal dominance deviation (how far C is from identity)\n276\t      mode_2: permutation component (which off-diagonal entries dominate)\n277\t  result_rationale: 'K=5,7 的 match rate 低于 K=3（0.89/0.85 vs 0.917）因为 MC 方差随 C 的自由参数数\n278\t    K(K-1) 增长——K=5 有 20 个自由参数，K=7 有 42 个，\n279\t\n280\t    相同 MC replications 下 confidence interval 更宽。\n281\t\n282\t\n283\t    Eigendecomposition 的 top 2 modes 能解释 83–91% 方差，因为实际 confusion matrix 具有低有效秩结构：\n284\t\n285\t    主导误差模式是\"相邻类别混淆\"（语义相似的类别被混淆），产生带对角扰动结构，被 2–3 个 eigenmodes 良好捕获。\n286\t\n287\t    Mediation 的方差解释率略低（0.83 K=5）因为间接效应涉及乘积，放大了二阶 eigenmode 的贡献。\n288\t\n289\t\n290\t    Worst-case bounds 保守（median 2.6×）因为它们对给定 diagonal dominance 下所有 C 做极值优化，\n291\t\n292\t    包括实际罕见的对抗性配置。作为安全边界是可接受的——类似 E-values 的保守性。\n293\t\n294\t\n295\t    Violation rates 随 K 轻微上升（mediation 23% → 28% → 31%）因为更大的 K 增加了 off-diagonal confusion\n296\t    路径，\n297\t\n298\t    使 label permutation 更可能。Exposure 接近饱和（85% → 88% → 90%）。\n299\t\n300\t    '\n301\t  tables:\n302\t  - name: 'Eigendecomposition: Variance Explained by Top Modes'\n303\t    columns:\n304\t    - topology\n305\t    - K\n306\t    - mode_1\n307\t    - mode_2\n308\t    - mode_3\n309\t    - cumulative_top2\n310\t    - cumulative_top3\n311\t    rows:\n312\t    - - confounding\n313\t      - 5\n314\t      - 0.68\n315\t      - 0.19\n316\t      - 0.08\n317\t      - 0.87\n318\t      - 0.95\n319\t    - - confounding\n320\t      - 7\n321\t      - 0.59\n322\t      - 0.17\n323\t      - 0.08\n324\t      - 0.76\n325\t      - 0.84\n326\t    - - exposure\n327\t      - 5\n328\t      - 0.74\n329\t      - 0.17\n330\t      - 0.05\n331\t      - 0.91\n332\t      - 0.96\n333\t    - - exposure\n334\t      - 7\n335\t      - 0.65\n336\t      - 0.15\n337\t      - 0.08\n338\t      - 0.8\n339\t      - 0.88\n340\t    - - mediation\n341\t      - 5\n342\t      - 0.61\n343\t      - 0.22\n344\t      - 0.09\n345\t      - 0.83\n346\t      - 0.92\n347\t    - - mediation\n348\t      - 7\n349\t      - 0.52\n350\t      - 0.19\n351\t      - 0.09\n352\t      - 0.71\n353\t      - 0.8\n354\t    - - collider\n355\t      - 5\n356\t      - 0.7\n357\t      - 0.18\n358\t      - 0.06\n359\t      - 0.88\n360\t      - 0.94\n361\t    - - collider\n362\t      - 7\n363\t      - 0.62\n364\t      - 0.16\n365\t      - 0.07\n366\t      - 0.78\n367\t      - 0.85\n368\t  - name: Violation Rate Scaling with K\n369\t    columns:\n370\t    - topology\n371\t    - K=3\n372\t    - K=5\n373\t    - K=7\n374\t    - trend\n375\t    rows:\n376\t    - - exposure\n377\t      - 0.85\n378\t      - 0.88\n379\t      - 0.9\n380\t      - near saturation\n381\t    - - mediation\n382\t      - 0.23\n383\t      - 0.28\n384\t      - 0.31\n385\t      - monotonic increase\n386\t    - - confounding\n387\t      - 0.0\n388\t      - 0.0\n389\t      - 0.0\n390\t      - flat (monotonic)\n391\t    - - collider\n392\t      - 0.0\n393\t      - 0.0\n394\t      - 0.0\n395\t      - flat (monotonic)\n396\t  figures_description:\n397\t  - 'Fig 5: Eigenspectrum bar charts — eigenvalue magnitude by mode index，各 topology\n398\t    at K=3,5,7。快速衰减，elbow 在 mode 2 (K=3,5) 或 mode 3 (K=7)。'\n399\t  - 'Fig 6: Bias magnitude scaling — K on x-axis，mean + 95th percentile bias on y-axis，一条线/topology。Exposure/mediation\n400\t    单调增长，其余平缓。'\n401\t  - 'Fig 7: Diagnostic heatmap — 5×5 C 的 diagonal dominance vs largest off-diagonal\n402\t    映射到预测 bias 量级。toolkit 交互版。'\n403\t  analysis: 'Matrix-form 表达式成功泛化 K=3 结果。实用发现：top 2 eigenmodes 在 K≤5 下足够（>83% 方差解释），\n404\t\n405\t    K=7 可能需要 3 个 modes。这指导 toolkit 设计——默认 2-mode summary 加可选扩展。\n406\t\n407\t    Reversal patterns 在 K=5,7 持续，确认 K=3 理论分析不是 special case。\n408\t\n409\t    Worst-case bounds 的保守性（2.6×）是 tradeoff：tight bounds 需要 topology-specific 优化（随\n410\t    K 扩展性差），\n411\t\n412\t    conservative bounds 计算快且作为安全边界仍有实用价值。\n413\t\n414\t    '\n415\t- name: 'Empirical Confusion Matrices: 3 LLMs × 3 CSS Tasks'\n416\t  plan_id: plan_003\n417\t  description: '从 Llama 4 Maverick, Qwen 3.5 Plus, DeepSeek V4 收集经验 confusion matrices。\n418\t\n419\t    3 个 CSS 任务：protest event coding (K=5, ACLED), stance detection (K=3, SemEval/VAST),\n420\t    toxicity (K=2, Civil Comments)。\n421\t\n422\t    ~30K annotations/model × 3 tasks × 3 prompt variants = ~270K total annotations。\n423\t\n424\t    '\n425\t  expected_results:\n426\t    api_cost_actual: $420\n427\t    total_annotations: 270000\n428\t    protest_K5:\n429\t      llama4_macro_f1: 0.71\n430\t      llama4_accuracy: 0.74\n431\t      qwen35_macro_f1: 0.68\n432\t      qwen35_accuracy: 0.71\n433\t      deepseek_macro_f1: 0.73\n434\t      deepseek_accuracy: 0.76\n435\t      inter_model_error_agreement: 0.58\n436\t      downstream_bias_range_abs:\n437\t      - 0.05\n438\t      - 0.12\n439\t      dominant_error_pattern: adjacent-category confusion (riot↔protest, strategic↔organized)\n440\t    stance_K3:\n441\t      llama4_macro_f1: 0.76\n442\t      llama4_accuracy: 0.79\n443\t      qwen35_macro_f1: 0.74\n444\t      qwen35_accuracy: 0.77\n445\t      deepseek_macro_f1: 0.78\n446\t      deepseek_accuracy: 0.81\n447\t      inter_model_error_agreement: 0.62\n448\t      downstream_bias_range_abs:\n449\t      - 0.03\n450\t      - 0.08\n451\t      dominant_error_pattern: neutral-as-default bias (favor→neutral, against→neutral)\n452\t    toxicity_K2:\n453\t      llama4_f1: 0.88\n454\t      llama4_accuracy: 0.9\n455\t      qwen35_f1: 0.86\n456\t      qwen35_accuracy: 0.88\n457\t      deepseek_f1: 0.89\n458\t      deepseek_accuracy: 0.91\n459\t      inter_model_error_agreement: 0.64\n460\t      downstream_bias_range_abs:\n461\t      - 0.01\n462\t      - 0.04\n463\t      dominant_error_pattern: slight FN bias (under-flagging toxicity)\n464\t    prompt_variant_stability: macro-F1 varies ±0.03; confusion matrix structure stable\n465\t      across prompts\n466\t    cross_model_error_correlation_mean: 0.61\n467\t  result_rationale: '性能水平反映 2025–2026 LLMs 在 CSS 任务上的典型表现：K=5 protest coding 最难（事件类型间区分微妙），\n468\t\n469\t    K=3 stance 中等（neutral 类别歧义性高），K=2 toxicity 最易（信号明确）。\n470\t\n471\t\n472\t    Inter-model error agreement（0.58–0.64）与 Kim et al.（ICML 2025）报告的 ~60% 一致。\n473\t\n474\t    Toxicity 略高因为 binary task 出错方式更少。\n475\t\n476\t    这验证了论文的动机前提：LLM errors are correlated，ensemble averaging 效果有限。\n477\t\n478\t\n479\t    Downstream bias 范围是中等的（非 dramatic）因为真实 LLM confusion matrices 是 moderately diagonal-dominant\n480\t    的——\n481\t\n482\t    不是 near-permutation 极端。这是 median 档的预期：理论极端（near-permutation C 导致 2.83× severity）\n483\t\n484\t    在当前 LLMs 中不会实际出现，但 bias 是可检测的且非 trivial 的。\n485\t\n486\t\n487\t    Prompt variant 稳定性（±0.03 F1，C structure stable）支持论文聚焦于 confusion matrix structure\n488\t    而非 prompt engineering——\n489\t\n490\t    error 的结构模式对 prompting 鲁棒，即使边际性能有移动。\n491\t\n492\t    '\n493\t  tables:\n494\t  - name: Empirical Performance Summary\n495\t    columns:\n496\t    - task\n497\t    - K\n498\t    - model\n499\t    - macro_F1\n500\t    - accuracy\n501\t    - dominant_error\n502\t    rows:\n503\t    - - protest\n504\t      - 5\n505\t      - Llama 4 Maverick\n506\t      - 0.71\n507\t      - 0.74\n508\t      - riot↔protest (0.15)\n509\t    - - protest\n510\t      - 5\n511\t      - Qwen 3.5 Plus\n512\t      - 0.68\n513\t      - 0.71\n514\t      - riot↔protest (0.18), remote↔organized (0.12)\n515\t    - - protest\n516\t      - 5\n517\t      - DeepSeek V4\n518\t      - 0.73\n519\t      - 0.76\n520\t      - riot↔protest (0.13)\n521\t    - - stance\n522\t      - 3\n523\t      - Llama 4 Maverick\n524\t      - 0.76\n525\t      - 0.79\n526\t      - favor→neutral (0.18)\n527\t    - - stance\n528\t      - 3\n529\t      - Qwen 3.5 Plus\n530\t      - 0.74\n531\t      - 0.77\n532\t      - favor→neutral (0.21), against→neutral (0.14)\n533\t    - - stance\n534\t      - 3\n535\t      - DeepSeek V4\n536\t      - 0.78\n537\t      - 0.81\n538\t      - favor→neutral (0.15)\n539\t    - - toxicity\n540\t      - 2\n541\t      - Llama 4 Maverick\n542\t      - 0.88\n543\t      - 0.9\n544\t      - FN toxic→non-toxic (0.12)\n545\t    - - toxicity\n546\t      - 2\n547\t      - Qwen 3.5 Plus\n548\t      - 0.86\n549\t      - 0.88\n550\t      - FN toxic→non-toxic (0.14)\n551\t    - - toxicity\n552\t      - 2\n553\t      - DeepSeek V4\n554\t      - 0.89\n555\t      - 0.91\n556\t      - FN toxic→non-toxic (0.10)\n557\t  - name: Inter-Model Error Correlation\n558\t    columns:\n559\t    - task\n560\t    - model_pair\n561\t    - error_agreement_when_both_err\n562\t    - kappa_on_errors\n563\t    rows:\n564\t    - - protest\n565\t      - Llama4–Qwen35\n566\t      - 0.56\n567\t      - 0.31\n568\t    - - protest\n569\t      - Llama4–DeepSeek\n570\t      - 0.61\n571\t      - 0.38\n572\t    - - protest\n573\t      - Qwen35–DeepSeek\n574\t      - 0.57\n575\t      - 0.33\n576\t    - - stance\n577\t      - Llama4–Qwen35\n578\t      - 0.6\n579\t      - 0.35\n580\t    - - stance\n581\t      - Llama4–DeepSeek\n582\t      - 0.64\n583\t      - 0.41\n584\t    - - stance\n585\t      - Qwen35–DeepSeek\n586\t      - 0.62\n587\t      - 0.37\n588\t    - - toxicity\n589\t      - Llama4–Qwen35\n590\t      - 0.63\n591\t      - 0.39\n592\t    - - toxicity\n593\t      - Llama4–DeepSeek\n594\t      - 0.66\n595\t      - 0.44\n596\t    - - toxicity\n597\t      - Qwen35–DeepSeek\n598\t      - 0.64\n599\t      - 0.41\n600\t  figures_description:\n601\t  - 'Fig 8: Confusion matrix heatmaps — 3×3 grid (models × tasks)，empirical C matrices\n602\t    with magnitude coloring。Adjacent-category confusion 在 protest K=5 可见，neutral-absorbing\n603\t    在 stance K=3 可见。'\n604\t  - 'Fig 9: Inter-model error scatter — per task，scatter of (model_A error, model_B\n605\t    error) per sample，colored by agreement。显示 correlation clustering。'\n606\t  - 'Fig 10: Downstream bias bar chart — gold-standard effect vs LLM-annotated effect\n607\t    for 9 model-task pairs。Bootstrap error bars。Bias 可见但不极端。'\n608\t  analysis: '经验 confusion matrices 确认真实 LLMs 产生 moderately diagonal-dominant 的 C matrix——\n609\t\n610\t    远离 near-permutation 极端但有足够 off-diagonal mass 产生可检测的 downstream bias。\n611\t\n612\t    关键经验发现：C structure 是 task-dependent（adjacent-category for protest，neutral-absorbing\n613\t    for stance）\n614\t\n615\t    且 model-stable（同一 task 下 3 个模型展示相似结构模式）。\n616\t\n617\t    这意味着理论 taxonomy 的 per-topology 预测适用于真实 LLM 场景——C structure 可从 task 预测，不取决于模型选择。\n618\t\n619\t    Inter-model error correlation 直接支持论文 framing：ensembles 无法修复系统性误差。\n620\t\n621\t    '\n622\t- name: Binarization Collapse Analysis Across 6 Topologies\n623\t  plan_id: plan_008\n624\t  description: '对 6 个拓扑在 K=3,5,7 下：将 K-class 变量折叠为 binary，\n625\t\n626\t    比较 full multi-class bias expression vs binarized expression。\n627\t\n628\t    评估何时 binarization 安全、何时危险。\n629\t\n630\t    '\n631\t  expected_results:\n632\t    max_delta_overall: 0.13\n633\t    max_delta_by_K:\n634\t      K3: 0.103\n635\t      K5: 0.13\n636\t      K7: 0.13\n637\t    worst_delta_topology: mediation (K=5)\n638\t    binarization_direction_reversal_topologies:\n639\t    - exposure\n640\t    - mediation\n641\t    safe_binarization_topologies:\n642\t    - collider\n643\t    - M-bias\n644\t    - instrument\n645\t    lossy_but_direction_safe:\n646\t    - confounding\n647\t    - front-door\n648\t    delta_by_topology_K3:\n649\t      confounding: 0.103\n650\t      mediation: 0.09\n651\t      collider: 0.07\n652\t      mbias: 0.06\n653\t      instrument: 0.05\n654\t      frontdoor: 0.08\n655\t    delta_by_topology_K5:\n656\t      confounding: 0.11\n657\t      mediation: 0.13\n658\t      collider: 0.09\n659\t      mbias: 0.08\n660\t      instrument: 0.06\n661\t      frontdoor: 0.09\n662\t  result_rationale: 'Binarization delta 在 K=5 达到峰值（0.13）并在 K=7 持平，因为 K→2 的信息损失在 K=5–7\n663\t    饱和——\n664\t\n665\t    超过 K=7 后额外类别的边际信息递减。\n666\t\n667\t\n668\t    Mediation 的 delta 最大（K=5 时 0.13）因为 binarizing mediator M 将间接路径折叠为单一对比，\n669\t\n670\t    丢失了 multi-class expression 捕获的 category-specific indirect effects。\n671\t\n672\t    对 exposure 和 mediation，某些 binarization folding 产生方向反转：\n673\t\n674\t    将 category 1+2 vs 3 折叠可能将相反方向的效应分配到同一 binary class。\n675\t\n676\t\n677\t    Confounding delta 高（K=3 0.103，来自 MVP）因为 binarizing confounder 丢失了残差混杂控制。\n678\t\n679\t    但方向保持（direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe）。\n680\t\n681\t\n682\t    Collider/M-bias/instrument delta 较小因为这些拓扑涉及辅助变量，\n683\t\n684\t    binary 近似更接近 multi-class truth——关键量（induced bias direction）更依赖 conditioning operation\n685\t    而非变量粒度。\n686\t\n687\t    '\n688\t  tables:\n689\t  - name: Binarization Delta Summary\n690\t    columns:\n691\t    - topology\n692\t    - K\n693\t    - max_delta\n694\t    - direction_reversal_from_binarization\n695\t    - safety_class\n696\t    rows:\n697\t    - - confounding\n698\t      - 3\n699\t      - 0.103\n700\t      - false\n701\t      - direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe\n702\t    - - confounding\n703\t      - 5\n704\t      - 0.11\n705\t      - false\n706\t      - direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe\n707\t    - - mediation\n708\t      - 3\n709\t      - 0.09\n710\t      - true\n711\t      - unsafe\n712\t    - - mediation\n713\t      - 5\n714\t      - 0.13\n715\t      - true\n716\t      - unsafe\n717\t    - - exposure (ref)\n718\t      - 3\n719\t      - 0.09\n720\t      - true\n721\t      - unsafe\n722\t    - - exposure (ref)\n723\t      - 5\n724\t      - 0.1\n725\t      - true\n726\t      - unsafe\n727\t    - - collider\n728\t      - 3\n729\t      - 0.07\n730\t      - false\n731\t      - safe\n732\t    - - collider\n733\t      - 5\n734\t      - 0.09\n735\t      - false\n736\t      - safe\n737\t    - - M-bias\n738\t      - 3\n739\t      - 0.06\n740\t      - false\n741\t      - safe\n742\t    - - instrument\n743\t      - 3\n744\t      - 0.05\n745\t      - false\n746\t      - safe\n747\t    - - front-door\n748\t      - 3\n749\t      - 0.08\n750\t      - false\n751\t      - direction-safe, magnitude-marginal\n752\t  figures_description:\n753\t  - 'Fig 11: Delta bar chart — grouped by topology，colored by K。Mediation 为最差 case，monotonic\n754\t    topologies 偏低。'\n755\t  - 'Fig 12: Binarization reversal case studies — 2 panels showing K=3 estimate (correct\n756\t    direction) vs binary estimate (reversed) for exposure and mediation，with specific\n757\t    C matrix and folding scheme。'\n758\t  analysis: 'Binarization 不是逃离 K≥3 复杂性的安全手段。Max delta 0.13（mediation K=5）在典型 CSS 回归中\n759\t\n760\t    （effect size 0.1–0.5）足以主导估计。\n761\t\n762\t    拓扑分三组：(1) binarization-unsafe（exposure, mediation——可能反转方向），\n763\t\n764\t    (2) binarization-lossy（confounding, front-door——保持方向但损失量级精度），\n765\t\n766\t    (3) binarization-tolerable（collider, M-bias, instrument——delta 小，安全）。\n767\t\n768\t    这支持论文的 multi-class treatment is necessary 论点。\n769\t\n770\t    '\n771\t- name: 'ASV Framework: Formal Proofs for Confounding, Mediation, Collider'\n772\t  plan_id: plan_004\n773\t  description: '推导 3 个优先拓扑的 ASV 表达式。形式化证明 monotonicity 和 sharpness。\n774\t\n775\t    MC 验证：coverage at 90%, 95%, 99% across 1000 scenarios/topology。\n776\t\n777\t    '\n778\t  expected_results:\n779\t    monotonicity_proved:\n780\t    - confounding\n781\t    - mediation\n782\t    - collider\n783\t    sharpness_proved:\n784\t    - confounding\n785\t    - mediation\n786\t    sharpness_incomplete:\n787\t    - collider\n788\t    sharpness_formal_proofs_count: 2\n789\t    collider_sharpness_numerical: achieving 93% of bound in 10k optimization runs\n790\t    coverage_at_95_nominal:\n791\t      confounding: 0.93\n792\t      mediation: 0.9\n793\t      collider: 0.91\n794\t    coverage_at_90_nominal:\n795\t      confounding: 0.95\n796\t      mediation: 0.92\n797\t      collider: 0.93\n798\t    coverage_at_99_nominal:\n799\t      confounding: 0.97\n800\t      mediation: 0.96\n801\t      collider: 0.95\n802\t    average_coverage_95: 0.913\n803\t  result_rationale: 'Monotonicity 对所有 3 个拓扑成立（proved）因为：更大的 δ 意味着 sensitivity set\n804\t    中考虑更极端的 C →\n805\t\n806\t    overturn conclusion 所需的 minimum perturbation 只能增加或不变。\n807\t\n808\t    这与 underlying bias 是否单调无关——ASV 是 min-over-C 量，不是 pointwise bias。\n809\t\n810\t\n811\t    Confounding sharpness：bias 在 C 的 off-diagonal elements 上是线性的，supremum 有 clean\n812\t    convex structure，\n813\t\n814\t    sharpness-achieving C 在 feasible set 的顶点。构造性证明。\n815\t\n816\t\n817\t    Mediation sharpness：尽管存在方向反转，ASV sharpness 仍可证——通过分别分析 attenuation regime 和 reversal\n818\t    regime。\n819\t\n820\t    Reversal boundary 处的 worst-case C 恰好达到 bound——构造性证明利用 phase transition 结构。\n821\t\n822\t    这是一个 nice 的结果：有反转的拓扑仍然有 tight bound，加强了 ASV 框架的可信度。\n823\t\n824\t\n825\t    Collider sharpness INCOMPLETE：bias 表达式涉及 conditioning on misclassified Z，\n826\t\n827\t    产生 E[Y|X,Z*] = Σ_z P(Z=z|Z*) E[Y|X,Z=z]。\n828\t\n829\t    对 C 做 supremum 要求联合优化 P(Z=z|Z*)，subject to C 为 valid confusion matrix，\n830\t\n831\t    产生非凸 bilinear 约束。数值优化达到 analytical bound 的 93%，强烈暗示 sharpness，\n832\t\n833\t    但形式化证明 supremum is attained 被 feasible set 的非凸拓扑阻断。\n834\t\n835\t\n836\t    Coverage 略低于 nominal（average 91.3% at 95% nominal）因为 ASV bounds 在已知 exact C 下推导，\n837\t\n838\t    而 MC 用的是有限样本估计的 C。Gap（3.7%）反映估计不确定性而非 bound failure。\n839\t\n840\t    '\n841\t  tables:\n842\t  - name: ASV Proof Status and Coverage (Priority Topologies)\n843\t    columns:\n844\t    - topology\n845\t    - monotonicity\n846\t    - sharpness\n847\t    - coverage_90\n848\t    - coverage_95\n849\t    - coverage_99\n850\t    rows:\n851\t    - - confounding\n852\t      - formal proof\n853\t      - formal proof\n854\t      - 0.95\n855\t      - 0.93\n856\t      - 0.97\n857\t    - - mediation\n858\t      - formal proof\n859\t      - formal proof\n860\t      - 0.92\n861\t      - 0.9\n862\t      - 0.96\n863\t    - - collider\n864\t      - formal proof\n865\t      - numerical only (93%)\n866\t      - 0.93\n867\t      - 0.91\n868\t      - 0.95\n869\t  figures_description:\n870\t  - 'Fig 13: ASV curves — ASV vs δ for 3 topologies，with MC pointwise confidence bands。Monotonicity\n871\t    直观可见。Mediation 曲线斜率更陡（对 amplification 更敏感）。'\n872\t  - 'Fig 14: Coverage calibration plots — nominal level (x) vs empirical coverage\n873\t    (y)。全部略低于对角线（mildly anti-conservative），confounding 最接近校准。'\n874\t  - 'Fig 15: Sharpness illustration — confounding + mediation 展示 achieving C matrix\n875\t    + bound value；collider 展示 best numerical C 与 analytical bound 的 gap。'\n876\t  analysis: 'ASV 框架在 3 个优先拓扑上验证：monotonicity universally proved，sharpness 2/3 proved。\n877\t\n878\t    Collider sharpness gap（7%）是主要技术障碍——论文应增加一段讨论 conditioning-on-misclassified-variable\n879\t    导致的非凸优化问题，\n880\t\n881\t    并标记 convex relaxation approach 为 future work。\n882\t\n883\t    Mediation 的更陡 ASV 曲线意味着 mediation DAGs 的结论对 annotation error 更敏感——\n884\t\n885\t    与 direction reversal 发现一致，自然连接 Claim 1 和 Claim 2。\n886\t\n887\t    '\n888\t- name: ASV MC Validation for M-bias, Instrument, Front-door\n889\t  plan_id: plan_005\n890\t  description: '推导剩余 3 个拓扑的 ASV 表达式 + MC 验证。\n891\t\n892\t    Monotonicity 和 coverage 验证。Sharpness 作为 conjectures + numerical evidence。\n893\t\n894\t    '\n895\t  expected_results:\n896\t    monotonicity_holds:\n897\t    - M-bias\n898\t    - instrument\n899\t    - front-door\n900\t    monotonicity_failures: 0\n901\t    sharpness_numerical:\n902\t      mbias: achieving 92% of bound\n903\t      instrument: achieving 89% of bound\n904\t      frontdoor: achieving 94% of bound\n905\t    coverage_at_95_nominal:\n906\t      mbias: 0.9\n907\t      instrument: 0.89\n908\t      frontdoor: 0.91\n909\t    instrument_conservatism: ASV bounds 1.8× wider than necessary\n910\t    total_asv_coverage_6_topologies: 0.907\n911\t  result_rationale: 'Monotonicity 对所有 3 个拓扑成立——与 plan_004 相同的结构性论证：\n912\t\n913\t    ASV 是 minimum-over-perturbation 量，在 perturbation budget δ 中固有单调。\n914\t\n915\t\n916\t    Sharpness numerical evidence 有差异：front-door 最接近 tight（94%，identification structure\n917\t    较简单），\n918\t\n919\t    M-bias 中等（92%），instrument 最远（89%）。\n920\t\n921\t    Instrument gap 反映 Wald estimator 的 ratio structure——supremum 涉及优化 misclassified\n922\t    量的 ratio，\n923\t\n924\t    landscape 有多个 local optima。\n925\t\n926\t\n927\t    Instrument ASV 显著保守（1.8× wider）因为 Wald estimator 放大小分母扰动，\n928\t\n929\t    worst-case bound 比 typical case 差很多。这是 IV sensitivity analysis 的已知问题（非本框架特有）。\n930\t\n931\t    '\n932\t  tables:\n933\t  - name: ASV Results for Secondary Topologies\n934\t    columns:\n935\t    - topology\n936\t    - monotonicity\n937\t    - sharpness_numerical_pct\n938\t    - coverage_95\n939\t    - conservatism\n940\t    rows:\n941\t    - - M-bias\n942\t      - holds\n943\t      - 92%\n944\t      - 0.9\n945\t      - comparable to collider\n946\t    - - instrument\n947\t      - holds\n948\t      - 89%\n949\t      - 0.89\n950\t      - 1.8× conservative (Wald ratio)\n951\t    - - front-door\n952\t      - holds\n953\t      - 94%\n954\t      - 0.91\n955\t      - near-tight\n956\t  - name: All 6 Topologies ASV Summary\n957\t    columns:\n958\t    - topology\n959\t    - monotonicity\n960\t    - sharpness_status\n961\t    - coverage_95\n962\t    rows:\n963\t    - - confounding\n964\t      - proved\n965\t      - proved (formal)\n966\t      - 0.93\n967\t    - - mediation\n968\t      - proved\n969\t      - proved (formal)\n970\t      - 0.9\n971\t    - - collider\n972\t      - proved\n973\t      - 93% numerical\n974\t      - 0.91\n975\t    - - M-bias\n976\t      - proved\n977\t      - 92% numerical\n978\t      - 0.9\n979\t    - - instrument\n980\t      - proved\n981\t      - 89% numerical\n982\t      - 0.89\n983\t    - - front-door\n984\t      - proved\n985\t      - 94% numerical\n986\t      - 0.91\n987\t  figures_description:\n988\t  - 'Fig 16: ASV curves for secondary topologies — same format as Fig 13。Instrument\n989\t    曲线显著更宽（更保守）。'\n990\t  - 'Fig 17: Sharpness gap comparison — 6 topologies bar chart of (1 − numerical_achievement/bound)。Confounding\n991\t    + mediation at 0% (proved)，others at 6–11%。'\n992\t  analysis: '6 个拓扑全部有 ASV 表达式 + validated monotonicity。Sharpness landscape：\n993\t\n994\t    2 proved (confounding, mediation) + 4 numerical (collider 93%, front-door 94%,\n995\t    M-bias 92%, instrument 89%)。\n996\t\n997\t    Instrument 是最弱环节——ASV 保守性限制了实用性。论文应诚实讨论并标记 tighter instrument-specific bounds\n998\t    为 future work。\n999\t\n1000\t    Overall average 95%-nominal coverage = 0.907，在 median 档 [0.88, 0.93] 范围内。\n1001\t\n1002\t    '\n1003\t- name: ASV Calibration on Empirical Data\n1004\t  plan_id: plan_006\n1005\t  description: '将 ASVs 应用于 plan_003 的经验 confusion matrices，跨 3 CSS tasks × 3 LLMs。\n1006\t\n1007\t    在 held-out gold-standard splits 上验证 coverage。\n1008\t\n1009\t    比较 ASV 可解释性与 raw confusion matrix reporting。\n1010\t\n1011\t    '\n1012\t  expected_results:\n1013\t    total_scenarios: 9\n1014\t    empirical_asv_concordance: 7\n1015\t    concordance_failures: 2\n1016\t    failure_scenarios:\n1017\t    - toxicity-Llama4 vs toxicity-Qwen35\n1018\t    - toxicity-Qwen35 vs toxicity-DeepSeek\n1019\t    failure_reason: all 3 models produce high ASVs (>2.0) for toxicity K=2; differences\n1020\t      within estimation noise\n1021\t    asv_ranking:\n1022\t      protest: DeepSeek (0.91) > Llama4 (0.82) > Qwen35 (0.68) — correct\n1023\t      stance: DeepSeek (1.41) > Llama4 (1.24) > Qwen35 (1.08) — correct\n1024\t      toxicity: DeepSeek (2.44) ≈ Llama4 (2.31) ≈ Qwen35 (2.18) — indistinguishable\n1025\t    held_out_coverage_95: 0.89\n1026\t  result_rationale: 'Concordance 7/9：ASV 在 protest (K=5) 和 stance (K=3) 任务上正确排序模型鲁棒性——\n1027\t\n1028\t    这些任务的 confusion matrix 差异足够大，产生有区分力的 ASV 值。\n1029\t\n1030\t    Failure 出现在 toxicity (K=2)：所有 3 个模型有 near-diagonal C（accuracy > 0.86），\n1031\t\n1032\t    产生高 ASVs (>2.0)，差异在 MC estimation noise 内——无法区分模型。\n1033\t\n1034\t\n1035\t    这是 low-bias regime 的结构性限制：annotation quality 高时（K=2 toxicity），\n1036\t\n1037\t    ASVs 正确指示\"robust\"但不能 rank-order models。\n1038\t\n1039\t    这实际上是合适的——如果所有模型产生 negligible bias，ranking 本身就无信息量。\n1040\t\n1041\t\n1042\t    Held-out coverage (0.89 at 95% nominal) 略低于 MC coverage (0.91) 因为 empirical C\n1043\t    有额外的\n1044\t\n1045\t    gold-standard sample size 估计噪声。Gap 小且在预期范围内。\n1046\t\n1047\t    '\n1048\t  tables:\n1049\t  - name: ASV Values and Concordance by Task × Model\n1050\t    columns:\n1051\t    - task\n1052\t    - model\n1053\t    - ASV_95\n1054\t    - observed_abs_bias\n1055\t    - robust_flag\n1056\t    - concordant\n1057\t    rows:\n1058\t    - - protest\n1059\t      - Llama 4\n1060\t      - 0.82\n1061\t      - 0.09\n1062\t      - moderate\n1063\t      - true\n1064\t    - - protest\n1065\t      - Qwen 3.5\n1066\t      - 0.68\n1067\t      - 0.12\n1068\t      - fragile\n1069\t      - true\n1070\t    - - protest\n1071\t      - DeepSeek\n1072\t      - 0.91\n1073\t      - 0.05\n1074\t      - moderate-high\n1075\t      - true\n1076\t    - - stance\n1077\t      - Llama 4\n1078\t      - 1.24\n1079\t      - 0.06\n1080\t      - moderate-high\n1081\t      - true\n1082\t    - - stance\n1083\t      - Qwen 3.5\n1084\t      - 1.08\n1085\t      - 0.08\n1086\t      - moderate\n1087\t      - true\n1088\t    - - stance\n1089\t      - DeepSeek\n1090\t      - 1.41\n1091\t      - 0.03\n1092\t      - high\n1093\t      - true\n1094\t    - - toxicity\n1095\t      - Llama 4\n1096\t      - 2.31\n1097\t      - 0.02\n1098\t      - high\n1099\t      - true\n1100\t    - - toxicity\n1101\t      - Qwen 3.5\n1102\t      - 2.18\n1103\t      - 0.04\n1104\t      - high\n1105\t      - false\n1106\t    - - toxicity\n1107\t      - DeepSeek\n1108\t      - 2.44\n1109\t      - 0.01\n1110\t      - high\n1111\t      - false\n1112\t  figures_description:\n1113\t  - 'Fig 18: ASV vs observed absolute bias scatter — 9 scenarios。Protest + stance\n1114\t    展示 negative correlation；toxicity 聚集在右上角（high ASV, low bias, indistinguishable）。'\n1115\t  - 'Fig 19: ASV vs raw C matrix comparison — side-by-side 对比 2 个 example scenarios，展示\n1116\t    ASV 提供 single interpretable number vs 9–25 cell matrix。'\n1117\t  analysis: 'ASVs 在 moderate-to-high bias scenarios 中具有经验实用性（protest K=5, stance K=3），\n1118\t\n1119\t    但在 low-bias regime 失去区分力（toxicity K=2）。这是诚实且预期的——\n1120\t\n1121\t    类似 E-values 在 confounding 小时不 informative。\n1122\t\n1123\t    论文应 frame 为：\"ASVs are most valuable when annotation error is non-trivial (K≥3,\n1124\t    accuracy <0.85)——\n1125\t\n1126\t    precisely the scenarios where researchers lack existing diagnostic tools。\"\n1127\t\n1128\t    7/9 concordance 支持 Claim 2 的实用价值。\n1129\t\n1130\t    '\n1131\t- name: 'Correction Guidance Framework: Decision Mapping and Validation'\n1132\t  plan_id: plan_007\n1133\t  description: 'Decision framework: {topology × error structure × ASV} → correction\n1134\t    method\n1135\t\n1136\t    (DSL / PPI / MLA / naive plug-in / \"no existing method adequate\")。\n1137\t\n1138\t    MC validation: 90 scenarios + empirical validation on plan_003 data。\n1139\t\n1140\t    '\n1141\t  expected_results:\n1142\t    total_mc_scenarios: 90\n1143\t    correction_framework_accuracy: 0.89\n1144\t    correct_recommendations: 80\n1145\t    boundary_indistinguishable_cases: 3\n1146\t    hard_failure_cases: 7\n1147\t    failure_breakdown:\n1148\t      near_diagonal_all_methods_equivalent: 3\n1149\t      differential_intermediate_mismatch: 2\n1150\t      false_recommendation_in_hopeless_regime: 2\n1151\t    method_dominance:\n1152\t      DSL: best in 28/90 (diagonal-dominant C, confounding/mediation)\n1153\t      PPI: best in 22/90 (moderate C, exposure/front-door)\n1154\t      MLA: best in 18/90 (high off-diagonal, confounding/collider)\n1155\t      naive_plugin: best in 12/90 (near-diagonal, any topology)\n1156\t      no_method_adequate: 10/90 (near-permutation + reversal topologies)\n1157\t    empirical_validation_plan003:\n1158\t      protest_correct: true\n1159\t      stance_correct: true\n1160\t      toxicity_correct: true\n1161\t    open_problems:\n1162\t    - dependence-aware multi-LLM correction\n1163\t    - differential K≥3 error correction\n1164\t    - collider + near-permutation C (no method reduces bias below 50%)\n1165\t  result_rationale: '89% accuracy 反映框架在 clear-cut scenarios（方法性能明显分离）的优势和 boundary\n1166\t    cases 的弱点。\n1167\t\n1168\t\n1169\t    3 个 boundary cases 是结构性不可区分的：near-diagonal C（low error）下所有方法结果相近（within 5%），\n1170\t\n1171\t    \"best\" recommendation 是任意的。这不是框架的失败而是问题本身的 degeneracy。\n1172\t\n1173\t\n1174\t    7 个 hard failures：\n1175\t\n1176\t    (a) 3 cases: near-diagonal C 使所有方法等效但框架因 threshold effects 选了次优方法；\n1177\t\n1178\t    (b) 2 cases: intermediate differential error 处框架的 non-differential/differential\n1179\t    二分类\n1180\t\n1181\t    无法捕获 differentiality 的连续性质；\n1182\t\n1183\t    (c) 2 cases: 框架推荐了方法但正确答案是\"no method adequate\"（near-permutation C + reversal topology）。\n1184\t\n1185\t\n1186\t    Method dominance 是 topology-driven 的：DSL 擅长 confounding（调整 misclassified confounder\n1187\t    是其 native use case），\n1188\t\n1189\t    PPI 擅长 exposure（regression-calibration 处理 treatment misclassification），\n1190\t\n1191\t    MLA 擅长 high off-diagonal error（maximum likelihood 直接建模 C）。\n1192\t\n1193\t\n1194\t    10/90 \"no method adequate\" 集中在 reversal topologies（exposure, mediation）+ extreme\n1195\t    C——\n1196\t\n1197\t    这些是 current correction literature 的真实 gaps。\n1198\t\n1199\t    '\n1200\t  tables:\n1201\t  - name: Correction Method Dominance Map\n1202\t    columns:\n1203\t    - method\n1204\t    - best_in_n\n1205\t    - primary_topology\n1206\t    - primary_error_regime\n1207\t    rows:\n1208\t    - - DSL\n1209\t      - 28\n1210\t      - confounding, mediation\n1211\t      - diagonal-dominant C\n1212\t    - - PPI\n1213\t      - 22\n1214\t      - exposure, front-door\n1215\t      - moderate off-diagonal\n1216\t    - - MLA\n1217\t      - 18\n1218\t      - confounding, collider\n1219\t      - high off-diagonal\n1220\t    - - naive plug-in\n1221\t      - 12\n1222\t      - any\n1223\t      - near-diagonal\n1224\t    - - no method\n1225\t      - 10\n1226\t      - exposure, mediation\n1227\t      - near-permutation\n1228\t  - name: Framework Failure Analysis\n1229\t    columns:\n1230\t    - failure_type\n1231\t    - count\n1232\t    - impact\n1233\t    - mitigation\n1234\t    rows:\n1235\t    - - boundary (methods ≤5% apart)\n1236\t      - 3\n1237\t      - low\n1238\t      - any recommendation acceptable\n1239\t    - - differential mismatch\n1240\t      - 2\n1241\t      - moderate\n1242\t      - add continuous differentiality parameter\n1243\t    - - false recommendation in hopeless regime\n1244\t      - 2\n1245\t      - high\n1246\t      - 'add safety check: if reversal topology + extreme C → flag'\n1247\t  figures_description:\n1248\t  - 'Fig 20: Decision tree / flowchart — {topology, error structure, ASV} → recommended\n1249\t    method。Color-coded by method，boundary regions highlighted。'\n1250\t  - 'Fig 21: Method accuracy heatmap — topology (rows) × error structure bins (cols)\n1251\t    → recommendation accuracy。Diagonal patterns showing topology-method alignment。'\n1252\t  - 'Fig 22: Open problems map — (off-diagonal mass, differentiality) 2D scatter colored\n1253\t    by adequate method existence。Gap region in upper-right clearly visible。'\n1254\t  analysis: 'Correction framework 达到主要目标：89% 正确识别 best correction method。\n1255\t\n1256\t    11% failure rate 集中在固有歧义的 boundary cases（3%）和真正困难的 regimes（8%）。\n1257\t\n1258\t    2 个\"false recommendation in hopeless regime\"最令人担忧——框架提供了虚假信心。\n1259\t\n1260\t    论文应明确讨论此风险并建议 practitioners 始终在 held-out data 上验证 corrections。\n1261\t\n1262\t    10 个\"no method adequate\"scenarios 是论文对 open problems 的贡献——\n1263\t\n1264\t    特别是 dependence-aware multi-LLM correction（结合 plan_003 的 correlation 发现）。\n1265\t\n1266\t    '\n1267\t- name: Pathological Confusion Matrix Analysis\n1268\t  plan_id: plan_009\n1269\t  description: '极端 C 结构分析：near-permutation, rank-deficient, block-diagonal。\n1270\t\n1271\t    刻画 catastrophic bias 条件并识别结构性预测因子。\n1272\t\n1273\t    '\n1274\t  expected_results:\n1275\t    spectral_gap_predictive_R2: 0.78\n1276\t    diagonal_dominance_predictive_R2: 0.71\n1277\t    combined_predictor_R2: 0.84\n1278\t    catastrophic_threshold_spectral_gap: 0.3\n1279\t    catastrophic_threshold_diagonal_dominance: 0.5\n1280\t    near_permutation_universally_catastrophic: true\n1281\t    rank_deficient_topology_dependent: true\n1282\t    rank_deficient_worst:\n1283\t    - front-door\n1284\t    - instrument\n1285\t    block_diagonal_worst: mediation (blocks indirect path)\n1286\t  result_rationale: 'Spectral gap（C 的第一和第二 eigenvalue 之差）预测 bias severity（R²=0.78）\n1287\t\n1288\t    因为它捕获了 C 距 permutation matrix 的距离——反转的结构性来源。\n1289\t\n1290\t    R²=0.78 表示强但不完美的预测；剩余方差来自 topology-specific interactions。\n1291\t\n1292\t\n1293\t    Diagonal dominance（minimum diagonal element）是更简单的 proxy，R² 略低（0.71）。\n1294\t\n1295\t    Combined spectral gap + diagonal dominance 达到 R²=0.84——两个 features 捕获了大部分 bias-relevant\n1296\t    C structure。\n1297\t\n1298\t\n1299\t    Near-permutation 普遍 catastrophic 因为 label-swapping 搅乱所有拓扑。\n1300\t\n1301\t    Rank-deficient C 是 topology-dependent：front-door 和 instrument 的 identification\n1302\t    formula\n1303\t\n1304\t    含有 C-dependent 分母——C rank-deficient 时分母趋零，bias unbounded。\n1305\t\n1306\t    Confounding/mediation/collider 对 rank deficiency 处理更 graceful（无 ratio estimator）。\n1307\t\n1308\t\n1309\t    Block-diagonal C 对 mediation 最 severe——block 结构可以创造 artifact category boundaries\n1310\t    上的 apparent indirect effects。\n1311\t\n1312\t    '\n1313\t  tables:\n1314\t  - name: Structural Predictors of Bias Severity\n1315\t    columns:\n1316\t    - predictor\n1317\t    - R2_overall\n1318\t    - best_topology_R2\n1319\t    - worst_topology_R2\n1320\t    rows:\n1321\t    - - spectral gap\n1322\t      - 0.78\n1323\t      - exposure (0.85)\n1324\t      - M-bias (0.67)\n1325\t    - - diagonal dominance\n1326\t      - 0.71\n1327\t      - confounding (0.82)\n1328\t      - front-door (0.58)\n1329\t    - - spectral gap + diag dom\n1330\t      - 0.84\n1331\t      - exposure (0.91)\n1332\t      - instrument (0.74)\n1333\t  - name: Catastrophic Bias Conditions by Topology and C Structure\n1334\t    columns:\n1335\t    - topology\n1336\t    - near_permutation\n1337\t    - rank_deficient\n1338\t    - block_diagonal\n1339\t    rows:\n1340\t    - - confounding\n1341\t      - severe (OVB > 2×)\n1342\t      - moderate\n1343\t      - moderate\n1344\t    - - exposure\n1345\t      - catastrophic (reversal)\n1346\t      - severe\n1347\t      - severe (block reversal)\n1348\t    - - mediation\n1349\t      - severe (reversal)\n1350\t      - moderate\n1351\t      - severe (block indirect effects)\n1352\t    - - collider\n1353\t      - severe (attenuation > 60%)\n1354\t      - moderate\n1355\t      - moderate\n1356\t    - - M-bias\n1357\t      - moderate\n1358\t      - moderate\n1359\t      - mild\n1360\t    - - instrument\n1361\t      - moderate\n1362\t      - catastrophic (Wald denom → 0)\n1363\t      - moderate\n1364\t    - - front-door\n1365\t      - moderate\n1366\t      - catastrophic (identification loss)\n1367\t      - moderate\n1368\t  figures_description:\n1369\t  - 'Fig 23: Spectral gap vs bias severity scatter — one panel/topology，threshold\n1370\t    at 0.3 where bias becomes catastrophic。'\n1371\t  - 'Fig 24: Phase diagram — spectral gap (x) × diagonal dominance (y) → bias regime\n1372\t    (safe/moderate/catastrophic)。Sharp boundaries visible。'\n1373\t  - 'Fig 25: Rank deficiency impact — bias magnitude vs effective matrix rank for\n1374\t    each topology。Front-door + instrument 在 rank 降低时 diverge。'\n1375\t  analysis: '实用 takeaway：spectral gap < 0.3 OR diagonal dominance < 0.5 → 所有拓扑均高风险。\n1376\t\n1377\t    这一双阈值规则足够简单可用且捕获 84% 的 bias variance。\n1378\t\n1379\t    Front-door 和 instrument 对 rank-deficient C 特别脆弱（ratio estimator 分母问题）。\n1380\t\n1381\t    这些 structural predictors 是 toolkit (plan_010) 的 automatic diagnostic features\n1382\t    候选。\n1383\t\n1384\t    '\n1385\t- name: annot-sensitivity Python Toolkit\n1386\t  plan_id: plan_010\n1387\t  description: 'Open-source pip-installable package：user-specified DAG + confusion\n1388\t    matrix + downstream estimate\n1389\t\n1390\t    → bias expressions + ASV + sensitivity curves + correction recommendation + diagnostic\n1391\t    plots。\n1392\t\n1393\t    '\n1394\t  expected_results:\n1395\t    package_name: annot-sensitivity\n1396\t    supported_topologies: 6\n1397\t    supported_K_range: 2–10\n1398\t    core_api:\n1399\t    - compute_bias(dag, C, estimate) → BiasResult\n1400\t    - compute_asv(dag, C, estimate, delta_range) → ASVResult\n1401\t    - recommend_correction(dag, C, asv) → CorrectionRecommendation\n1402\t    - diagnostic_plot(result) → Figure\n1403\t    - eigendecomp_summary(C, K) → EigenSummary\n1404\t    - check_pathological(C) → PathologyReport (spectral gap + diag dom thresholds)\n1405\t    worked_examples: 3\n1406\t    example_topologies:\n1407\t    - confounding (baseline)\n1408\t    - exposure (reversal)\n1409\t    - mediation (conditional reversal)\n1410\t    test_coverage: 0.87\n1411\t    documentation: API reference + 3 tutorial notebooks + quick-start guide\n1412\t    known_limitations:\n1413\t    - K>7 eigendecomposition slow (>10s/computation)\n1414\t    - correction accuracy inherits plan_007 limitations (89%)\n1415\t    - CLI + notebook only, no GUI\n1416\t    - 3/6 topologies lack detailed tutorials (M-bias, instrument, front-door)\n1417\t  result_rationale: '3 个 worked examples（而非 6）因为 median 档 scope 有限——优先覆盖 3 个 reversal-relevant\n1418\t    拓扑\n1419\t\n1420\t    （confounding 作为 baseline，exposure + mediation 作为反转案例）。剩余 3 个拓扑在 API 中支持但缺少详细 tutorial。\n1421\t\n1422\t\n1423\t    K>7 性能限制反映 eigendecomposition 的 O(K³) 成本——对典型 CSS 使用（K=3–7）可接受，\n1424\t\n1425\t    对罕见 high-K 应用偏慢。\n1426\t\n1427\t\n1428\t    Test coverage 0.87 反映核心计算（bias expressions, ASV）的 thorough unit testing\n1429\t\n1430\t    和 visualization/correction recommendation 组件的 lighter testing。\n1431\t\n1432\t\n1433\t    check_pathological() 集成 plan_009 的 spectral gap + diagonal dominance 阈值，\n1434\t\n1435\t    为 practitioner 提供自动 C matrix 质量诊断。\n1436\t\n1437\t    '\n1438\t  tables: []\n1439\t  figures_description:\n1440\t  - 'Fig 26 (toolkit demo): Notebook screenshot — exposure DAG K=3 的完整输出：bias expression,\n1441\t    ASV curve, correction recommendation, diagnostic plot，in a single cell。'\n1442\t  analysis: 'Toolkit 是 functional deliverable，使论文的理论贡献对 practitioners 可及。\n1443\t\n1444\t    3 个 worked examples 覆盖最重要的场景（reversal cases）。\n1445\t\n1446\t    主要 gap：3 个拓扑缺少 tutorial，可能限制 M-bias/instrument/front-door 用户的采纳。\n1447\t\n1448\t    Post-publication 低成本 follow-up。'\n1449\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44efd5d7-3d5f-464d-80ca-d3c01b5a58d8","uuid":"3f4cc120-0dad-4509-8f37-e4b489b1fe1d","timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:48:01.418Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-prod_0510/projects/causal_annot_error_attrib/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T074549/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Version A 成立但 scope 收窄至 2 个反转拓扑：exposure（MVP 已确认，violation rate\n  85%）+ mediation（plan_001 新发现，violation rate 23%，条件性反转——仅在 off-diagonal dominance\n  > 0.6 且 |indirect effect| > 0.2 时触发）。\n\n  其余 4 个拓扑（confounding, collider, M-bias, instrument, front-door）保持单调性，但 magnitude\n  变异显著（如 collider bias range 0.04–0.21）。\n\n  Lead finding 聚焦于 exposure vs mediation 的对比：exposure 反转是\"广泛性的\"（85%，几乎所有非对角 C），mediation\n  反转是\"条件性的\"（23%，需要双重门控）。这一对比本身就是核心贡献——同样的 non-differential error 在不同拓扑下产生质变差异。\n\n  Claim 1 调整：taxonomy 有效，但方向反转是 topology-specific 而非 universal；magnitude 不可预测性作为补充论据（所有\n  6 个拓扑均存在）。\n\n  Claim 2 调整：ASV 紧性降级为 2 个拓扑有形式化证明（confounding + mediation）+ 4 个有 MC 数值证据；增加一段讨论 collider\n  conditioning structure 导致优化非凸的技术障碍。\n\n  Claim 3 不变。\n\n  需补充实验：(1) 对 exposure 和 mediation 做 C structure 条件分析（反转边界的精确刻画——何时反转、何时不反转），(2) 增加\n  1 个经验任务（如 emotion detection K=6）以补偿理论覆盖面的缩窄，使经验证据更丰富。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: K=3 Bias Expressions and MC Validation Across 6 DAG Topologies\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: '对 6 个 DAG 拓扑（confounding, mediation, collider, M-bias, instrument,\n    front-door）推导 K=3 closed-form bias 表达式，\n\n    MC 验证：1000 reps × N=10000 × 6 confusion matrix structures/topology = 36 scenarios。\n\n    每个拓扑做 100k random C search 检测方向反转。Confounding 为 MVP 再验证；其余 5 个为新推导。\n\n    结合 MVP exposure 结果，total reversal topologies = 2。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_scenarios: 36\n    theory_mc_match: 33/36\n    theory_mc_match_rate: 0.917\n    reversal_in_plan_001: 1\n    reversal_topology_new: mediation\n    combined_reversal_topologies: 2\n    combined_reversal_list:\n    - exposure (MVP)\n    - mediation (new)\n    confounding:\n      violation_rate: 0.0\n      bias_range:\n      - 0.132\n      - 0.298\n      theory_mc: 6/6\n      mechanism: residual confounding, monotonic toward OVB\n    mediation:\n      violation_rate: 0.23\n      sign_reversal_rate: 0.18\n      amplification_rate: 0.05\n      worst_severity: 1.62\n      named_structures_with_violation: 2/6 (near-permutation, block-off-diagonal)\n      theory_mc: 6/6\n      reversal_condition: off-diagonal dominance > 0.6 AND |indirect effect| > 0.2\n      indirect_bias_range:\n      - -0.18\n      - 0.14\n    collider:\n      violation_rate: 0.0\n      bias_range:\n      - 0.04\n      - 0.21\n      attenuation_range: 15-60% reduction vs no misclassification\n      theory_mc: 5/6\n      mechanism: misclassification smooths conditioning variable, reduces collider\n        bias magnitude, preserves direction\n    mbias:\n      violation_rate: 0.0\n      bias_range:\n      - 0.02\n      - 0.16\n      theory_mc: 5/6\n      mechanism: spurious pathway weakened by misclassification of M-bias variable\n    instrument:\n      violation_rate: 0.0\n      bias_range:\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.19\n      theory_mc: 6/6\n      mechanism: instrument weakened, Wald estimator biased toward OLS, direction\n        preserved\n    frontdoor:\n      violation_rate: 0.0\n      bias_range:\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.22\n      theory_mc: 5/6\n      mechanism: front-door estimate attenuated, identification weakened but direction\n        stable\n    mc_mismatch_detail: 3 mismatches in collider(1), M-bias(1), front-door(1) — all\n      near-permutation C where MC variance is highest due to complex bias formulas\n      (conditioning, ratio estimators)\n  result_rationale: 'Mediation（23% violation）：misclassifying mediator M 影响间接路径 X→M→Y。反转需要双重门控：\n\n    (a) C matrix off-diagonal dominance > 0.6（标签大幅置换），AND (b) |true indirect effect|\n    > 0.2（间接效应足够大可以被反转）。\n\n    因为间接效应 = X→M 系数 × M→Y 系数的乘积，两条路径都必须被实质性扰动才能反转——这种双重门控将 violation rate 限制在 23%。\n\n    对比 exposure（MVP 85% violation）：exposure misclassification 直接作用于单一 X→Y 路径，无衰减机制，几乎所有非对角\n    C 都触发反转。\n\n    这一机制差异（直接路径 vs 乘积路径）是 median 档的核心发现——direction reversal 是 topology-specific 的。\n\n\n    Collider（0% violation）：misclassifying Z（collider）并 conditioning on Z* 时，误分类平滑了\n    Z 的分布，\n\n    削弱了 selection effect 的强度但不改变其方向。方向由结构方程的符号决定（与测量质量无关）。\n\n    100k random C 中无一例外。\n\n\n    M-bias/Instrument/Front-door（0% violation）：这些拓扑涉及辅助变量，misclassification 削弱 identification\n    但不反转估计方向。\n\n    Instrument 特殊之处在于 Wald estimator 的分母受影响（偏向 OLS），但符号不变。\n\n    Front-door 的 double summation 使 MC 方差在极端 C 下偏高，导致 1/6 mismatch。\n\n\n    3 个 MC mismatch 均出现在 near-permutation C structure 下——这些拓扑的 bias formula 含有 conditioning\n    或 ratio 结构，\n\n    MC 在极端 C 下方差更大，理论值落在 95% CI 边缘外。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Direction Reversal Summary by Topology (plan_001 + MVP exposure)\n    columns:\n    - topology\n    - misclassified_var\n    - violation_rate\n    - sign_reversal\n    - worst_severity\n    - theory_mc\n    - direction\n    rows:\n    - - exposure (MVP)\n      - treatment X\n      - 0.85\n      - 0.834\n      - 2.83\n      - 5/5\n      - reversal-dominant\n    - - confounding\n      - confounder U\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 1.00×OVB\n      - 6/6\n      - monotonic toward OVB\n    - - mediation\n      - mediator M\n      - 0.23\n      - 0.18\n      - 1.62\n      - 6/6\n      - conditional reversal\n    - - collider\n      - collider Z\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.85×(attenuated)\n      - 5/6\n      - monotonic attenuation\n    - - M-bias\n      - M-bias var\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.92×(attenuated)\n      - 5/6\n      - monotonic attenuation\n    - - instrument\n      - instrument Z\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.78×(toward OLS)\n      - 6/6\n      - monotonic toward OLS\n    - - front-door\n      - front-door M\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.88×(attenuated)\n      - 5/6\n      - monotonic attenuation\n  - name: Mediation Reversal Conditions (100k Random C, K=3)\n    columns:\n    - C_structure_category\n    - pct_of_random_C\n    - violation_rate\n    - sign_reversal_rate\n    rows:\n    - - near-permutation (off-diag dom > 0.6)\n      - 30%\n      - 0.57\n      - 0.44\n    - - moderate (off-diag dom 0.3–0.6)\n      - 40%\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.09\n    - - diagonal-dominant (off-diag dom < 0.3)\n      - 30%\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.0\n    - - overall\n      - 100%\n      - 0.23\n      - 0.18\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 1: Heatmap — topology (rows) × named C structure (cols) → bias magnitude\n    (color intensity) and direction (red=reversal, blue=toward-null). Exposure 行几乎全红，mediation\n    行 2/6 红，其余行全蓝。'\n  - 'Fig 2: Violin plots — 100k random C 下各 topology 的 bias 分布。Exposure 为跨零的宽双峰分布；mediation\n    右偏但有负值尾部；其余单峰正值。'\n  - 'Fig 3: Mediation 反转 phase diagram — off-diagonal dominance (x) × |indirect effect|\n    (y) → reversal probability (color). 在 dominance > 0.6、|indirect| > 0.2 处有清晰边界。'\n  analysis: 'plan_001 确认 median 档的核心结果：6 个拓扑中仅 mediation 出现新的反转（结合 MVP exposure =\n    2 个反转拓扑）。\n\n    关键发现是反转机制的不对称性：exposure 是\"广泛性反转\"（label swap 直接作用于 treatment 对比），\n\n    mediation 是\"条件性反转\"（需双重门控：C 足够非对角 + 间接效应足够大）。\n\n    这一不对称性本身就是论文的核心贡献——它证明了 direction reversal 是 topology-specific 的，\n\n    不能仅从 confusion matrix 结构预测，必须结合 DAG 拓扑分析。\n\n    4 个单调拓扑的 magnitude 变异（如 collider 0.04–0.21）支持补充论据：即使方向保持，\n\n    bias magnitude 仍不可从 binary 框架预测。\n\n    需要补充实验：对 mediation 的 phase diagram 做更精细的 grid search（Fig 3 的分辨率不够用于实用指导）。\n\n    '\n- name: General-K Matrix Bias Expressions and Interpretability Tools\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: '将 bias 表达式扩展到 K=5,7 的矩阵形式。开发 3 个可解释性工具：\n\n    (a) eigendecomposition summaries，(b) worst-case scalar bounds，(c) diagnostic visualizations。\n\n    在 confounding + mediation + collider + exposure DAGs 上验证 K=5,7。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    K5_theory_mc_match_rate: 0.89\n    K7_theory_mc_match_rate: 0.85\n    K5_scenarios_tested: 24\n    K7_scenarios_tested: 24\n    eigendecomp_variance_explained_top2_K5:\n      confounding: 0.87\n      exposure: 0.91\n      mediation: 0.83\n      collider: 0.88\n    eigendecomp_variance_explained_top3_K7:\n      confounding: 0.84\n      exposure: 0.88\n      mediation: 0.8\n      collider: 0.85\n    worst_case_bound_conservatism_median: 2.6×\n    worst_case_bound_conservatism_range: 2.1–3.4×\n    K5_exposure_violation_rate: 0.88\n    K5_mediation_violation_rate: 0.28\n    K7_exposure_violation_rate: 0.9\n    K7_mediation_violation_rate: 0.31\n    reversal_pattern_persistence: true\n    dominant_eigenmode_interpretation:\n      mode_1: diagonal dominance deviation (how far C is from identity)\n      mode_2: permutation component (which off-diagonal entries dominate)\n  result_rationale: 'K=5,7 的 match rate 低于 K=3（0.89/0.85 vs 0.917）因为 MC 方差随 C 的自由参数数\n    K(K-1) 增长——K=5 有 20 个自由参数，K=7 有 42 个，\n\n    相同 MC replications 下 confidence interval 更宽。\n\n\n    Eigendecomposition 的 top 2 modes 能解释 83–91% 方差，因为实际 confusion matrix 具有低有效秩结构：\n\n    主导误差模式是\"相邻类别混淆\"（语义相似的类别被混淆），产生带对角扰动结构，被 2–3 个 eigenmodes 良好捕获。\n\n    Mediation 的方差解释率略低（0.83 K=5）因为间接效应涉及乘积，放大了二阶 eigenmode 的贡献。\n\n\n    Worst-case bounds 保守（median 2.6×）因为它们对给定 diagonal dominance 下所有 C 做极值优化，\n\n    包括实际罕见的对抗性配置。作为安全边界是可接受的——类似 E-values 的保守性。\n\n\n    Violation rates 随 K 轻微上升（mediation 23% → 28% → 31%）因为更大的 K 增加了 off-diagonal confusion\n    路径，\n\n    使 label permutation 更可能。Exposure 接近饱和（85% → 88% → 90%）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Eigendecomposition: Variance Explained by Top Modes'\n    columns:\n    - topology\n    - K\n    - mode_1\n    - mode_2\n    - mode_3\n    - cumulative_top2\n    - cumulative_top3\n    rows:\n    - - confounding\n      - 5\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.87\n      - 0.95\n    - - confounding\n      - 7\n      - 0.59\n      - 0.17\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.84\n    - - exposure\n      - 5\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.17\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.96\n    - - exposure\n      - 7\n      - 0.65\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.88\n    - - mediation\n      - 5\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.83\n      - 0.92\n    - - mediation\n      - 7\n      - 0.52\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.8\n    - - collider\n      - 5\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.88\n      - 0.94\n    - - collider\n      - 7\n      - 0.62\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.07\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.85\n  - name: Violation Rate Scaling with K\n    columns:\n    - topology\n    - K=3\n    - K=5\n    - K=7\n    - trend\n    rows:\n    - - exposure\n      - 0.85\n      - 0.88\n      - 0.9\n      - near saturation\n    - - mediation\n      - 0.23\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.31\n      - monotonic increase\n    - - confounding\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.0\n      - flat (monotonic)\n    - - collider\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.0\n      - flat (monotonic)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 5: Eigenspectrum bar charts — eigenvalue magnitude by mode index，各 topology\n    at K=3,5,7。快速衰减，elbow 在 mode 2 (K=3,5) 或 mode 3 (K=7)。'\n  - 'Fig 6: Bias magnitude scaling — K on x-axis，mean + 95th percentile bias on y-axis，一条线/topology。Exposure/mediation\n    单调增长，其余平缓。'\n  - 'Fig 7: Diagnostic heatmap — 5×5 C 的 diagonal dominance vs largest off-diagonal\n    映射到预测 bias 量级。toolkit 交互版。'\n  analysis: 'Matrix-form 表达式成功泛化 K=3 结果。实用发现：top 2 eigenmodes 在 K≤5 下足够（>83% 方差解释），\n\n    K=7 可能需要 3 个 modes。这指导 toolkit 设计——默认 2-mode summary 加可选扩展。\n\n    Reversal patterns 在 K=5,7 持续，确认 K=3 理论分析不是 special case。\n\n    Worst-case bounds 的保守性（2.6×）是 tradeoff：tight bounds 需要 topology-specific 优化（随\n    K 扩展性差），\n\n    conservative bounds 计算快且作为安全边界仍有实用价值。\n\n    '\n- name: 'Empirical Confusion Matrices: 3 LLMs × 3 CSS Tasks'\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: '从 Llama 4 Maverick, Qwen 3.5 Plus, DeepSeek V4 收集经验 confusion matrices。\n\n    3 个 CSS 任务：protest event coding (K=5, ACLED), stance detection (K=3, SemEval/VAST),\n    toxicity (K=2, Civil Comments)。\n\n    ~30K annotations/model × 3 tasks × 3 prompt variants = ~270K total annotations。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    api_cost_actual: $420\n    total_annotations: 270000\n    protest_K5:\n      llama4_macro_f1: 0.71\n      llama4_accuracy: 0.74\n      qwen35_macro_f1: 0.68\n      qwen35_accuracy: 0.71\n      deepseek_macro_f1: 0.73\n      deepseek_accuracy: 0.76\n      inter_model_error_agreement: 0.58\n      downstream_bias_range_abs:\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.12\n      dominant_error_pattern: adjacent-category confusion (riot↔protest, strategic↔organized)\n    stance_K3:\n      llama4_macro_f1: 0.76\n      llama4_accuracy: 0.79\n      qwen35_macro_f1: 0.74\n      qwen35_accuracy: 0.77\n      deepseek_macro_f1: 0.78\n      deepseek_accuracy: 0.81\n      inter_model_error_agreement: 0.62\n      downstream_bias_range_abs:\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.08\n      dominant_error_pattern: neutral-as-default bias (favor→neutral, against→neutral)\n    toxicity_K2:\n      llama4_f1: 0.88\n      llama4_accuracy: 0.9\n      qwen35_f1: 0.86\n      qwen35_accuracy: 0.88\n      deepseek_f1: 0.89\n      deepseek_accuracy: 0.91\n      inter_model_error_agreement: 0.64\n      downstream_bias_range_abs:\n      - 0.01\n      - 0.04\n      dominant_error_pattern: slight FN bias (under-flagging toxicity)\n    prompt_variant_stability: macro-F1 varies ±0.03; confusion matrix structure stable\n      across prompts\n    cross_model_error_correlation_mean: 0.61\n  result_rationale: '性能水平反映 2025–2026 LLMs 在 CSS 任务上的典型表现：K=5 protest coding 最难（事件类型间区分微妙），\n\n    K=3 stance 中等（neutral 类别歧义性高），K=2 toxicity 最易（信号明确）。\n\n\n    Inter-model error agreement（0.58–0.64）与 Kim et al.（ICML 2025）报告的 ~60% 一致。\n\n    Toxicity 略高因为 binary task 出错方式更少。\n\n    这验证了论文的动机前提：LLM errors are correlated，ensemble averaging 效果有限。\n\n\n    Downstream bias 范围是中等的（非 dramatic）因为真实 LLM confusion matrices 是 moderately diagonal-dominant\n    的——\n\n    不是 near-permutation 极端。这是 median 档的预期：理论极端（near-permutation C 导致 2.83× severity）\n\n    在当前 LLMs 中不会实际出现，但 bias 是可检测的且非 trivial 的。\n\n\n    Prompt variant 稳定性（±0.03 F1，C structure stable）支持论文聚焦于 confusion matrix structure\n    而非 prompt engineering——\n\n    error 的结构模式对 prompting 鲁棒，即使边际性能有移动。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Empirical Performance Summary\n    columns:\n    - task\n    - K\n    - model\n    - macro_F1\n    - accuracy\n    - dominant_error\n    rows:\n    - - protest\n      - 5\n      - Llama 4 Maverick\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.74\n      - riot↔protest (0.15)\n    - - protest\n      - 5\n      - Qwen 3.5 Plus\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.71\n      - riot↔protest (0.18), remote↔organized (0.12)\n    - - protest\n      - 5\n      - DeepSeek V4\n      - 0.73\n      - 0.76\n      - riot↔protest (0.13)\n    - - stance\n      - 3\n      - Llama 4 Maverick\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.79\n      - favor→neutral (0.18)\n    - - stance\n      - 3\n      - Qwen 3.5 Plus\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.77\n      - favor→neutral (0.21), against→neutral (0.14)\n    - - stance\n      - 3\n      - DeepSeek V4\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.81\n      - favor→neutral (0.15)\n    - - toxicity\n      - 2\n      - Llama 4 Maverick\n      - 0.88\n      - 0.9\n      - FN toxic→non-toxic (0.12)\n    - - toxicity\n      - 2\n      - Qwen 3.5 Plus\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.88\n      - FN toxic→non-toxic (0.14)\n    - - toxicity\n      - 2\n      - DeepSeek V4\n      - 0.89\n      - 0.91\n      - FN toxic→non-toxic (0.10)\n  - name: Inter-Model Error Correlation\n    columns:\n    - task\n    - model_pair\n    - error_agreement_when_both_err\n    - kappa_on_errors\n    rows:\n    - - protest\n      - Llama4–Qwen35\n      - 0.56\n      - 0.31\n    - - protest\n      - Llama4–DeepSeek\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.38\n    - - protest\n      - Qwen35–DeepSeek\n      - 0.57\n      - 0.33\n    - - stance\n      - Llama4–Qwen35\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.35\n    - - stance\n      - Llama4–DeepSeek\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.41\n    - - stance\n      - Qwen35–DeepSeek\n      - 0.62\n      - 0.37\n    - - toxicity\n      - Llama4–Qwen35\n      - 0.63\n      - 0.39\n    - - toxicity\n      - Llama4–DeepSeek\n      - 0.66\n      - 0.44\n    - - toxicity\n      - Qwen35–DeepSeek\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.41\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 8: Confusion matrix heatmaps — 3×3 grid (models × tasks)，empirical C matrices\n    with magnitude coloring。Adjacent-category confusion 在 protest K=5 可见，neutral-absorbing\n    在 stance K=3 可见。'\n  - 'Fig 9: Inter-model error scatter — per task，scatter of (model_A error, model_B\n    error) per sample，colored by agreement。显示 correlation clustering。'\n  - 'Fig 10: Downstream bias bar chart — gold-standard effect vs LLM-annotated effect\n    for 9 model-task pairs。Bootstrap error bars。Bias 可见但不极端。'\n  analysis: '经验 confusion matrices 确认真实 LLMs 产生 moderately diagonal-dominant 的 C matrix——\n\n    远离 near-permutation 极端但有足够 off-diagonal mass 产生可检测的 downstream bias。\n\n    关键经验发现：C structure 是 task-dependent（adjacent-category for protest，neutral-absorbing\n    for stance）\n\n    且 model-stable（同一 task 下 3 个模型展示相似结构模式）。\n\n    这意味着理论 taxonomy 的 per-topology 预测适用于真实 LLM 场景——C structure 可从 task 预测，不取决于模型选择。\n\n    Inter-model error correlation 直接支持论文 framing：ensembles 无法修复系统性误差。\n\n    '\n- name: Binarization Collapse Analysis Across 6 Topologies\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: '对 6 个拓扑在 K=3,5,7 下：将 K-class 变量折叠为 binary，\n\n    比较 full multi-class bias expression vs binarized expression。\n\n    评估何时 binarization 安全、何时危险。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    max_delta_overall: 0.13\n    max_delta_by_K:\n      K3: 0.103\n      K5: 0.13\n      K7: 0.13\n    worst_delta_topology: mediation (K=5)\n    binarization_direction_reversal_topologies:\n    - exposure\n    - mediation\n    safe_binarization_topologies:\n    - collider\n    - M-bias\n    - instrument\n    lossy_but_direction_safe:\n    - confounding\n    - front-door\n    delta_by_topology_K3:\n      confounding: 0.103\n      mediation: 0.09\n      collider: 0.07\n      mbias: 0.06\n      instrument: 0.05\n      frontdoor: 0.08\n    delta_by_topology_K5:\n      confounding: 0.11\n      mediation: 0.13\n      collider: 0.09\n      mbias: 0.08\n      instrument: 0.06\n      frontdoor: 0.09\n  result_rationale: 'Binarization delta 在 K=5 达到峰值（0.13）并在 K=7 持平，因为 K→2 的信息损失在 K=5–7\n    饱和——\n\n    超过 K=7 后额外类别的边际信息递减。\n\n\n    Mediation 的 delta 最大（K=5 时 0.13）因为 binarizing mediator M 将间接路径折叠为单一对比，\n\n    丢失了 multi-class expression 捕获的 category-specific indirect effects。\n\n    对 exposure 和 mediation，某些 binarization folding 产生方向反转：\n\n    将 category 1+2 vs 3 折叠可能将相反方向的效应分配到同一 binary class。\n\n\n    Confounding delta 高（K=3 0.103，来自 MVP）因为 binarizing confounder 丢失了残差混杂控制。\n\n    但方向保持（direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe）。\n\n\n    Collider/M-bias/instrument delta 较小因为这些拓扑涉及辅助变量，\n\n    binary 近似更接近 multi-class truth——关键量（induced bias direction）更依赖 conditioning operation\n    而非变量粒度。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Binarization Delta Summary\n    columns:\n    - topology\n    - K\n    - max_delta\n    - direction_reversal_from_binarization\n    - safety_class\n    rows:\n    - - confounding\n      - 3\n      - 0.103\n      - false\n      - direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe\n    - - confounding\n      - 5\n      - 0.11\n      - false\n      - direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe\n    - - mediation\n      - 3\n      - 0.09\n      - true\n      - unsafe\n    - - mediation\n      - 5\n      - 0.13\n      - true\n      - unsafe\n    - - exposure (ref)\n      - 3\n      - 0.09\n      - true\n      - unsafe\n    - - exposure (ref)\n      - 5\n      - 0.1\n      - true\n      - unsafe\n    - - collider\n      - 3\n      - 0.07\n      - false\n      - safe\n    - - collider\n      - 5\n      - 0.09\n      - false\n      - safe\n    - - M-bias\n      - 3\n      - 0.06\n      - false\n      - safe\n    - - instrument\n      - 3\n      - 0.05\n      - false\n      - safe\n    - - front-door\n      - 3\n      - 0.08\n      - false\n      - direction-safe, magnitude-marginal\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 11: Delta bar chart — grouped by topology，colored by K。Mediation 为最差 case，monotonic\n    topologies 偏低。'\n  - 'Fig 12: Binarization reversal case studies — 2 panels showing K=3 estimate (correct\n    direction) vs binary estimate (reversed) for exposure and mediation，with specific\n    C matrix and folding scheme。'\n  analysis: 'Binarization 不是逃离 K≥3 复杂性的安全手段。Max delta 0.13（mediation K=5）在典型 CSS 回归中\n\n    （effect size 0.1–0.5）足以主导估计。\n\n    拓扑分三组：(1) binarization-unsafe（exposure, mediation——可能反转方向），\n\n    (2) binarization-lossy（confounding, front-door——保持方向但损失量级精度），\n\n    (3) binarization-tolerable（collider, M-bias, instrument——delta 小，安全）。\n\n    这支持论文的 multi-class treatment is necessary 论点。\n\n    '\n- name: 'ASV Framework: Formal Proofs for Confounding, Mediation, Collider'\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: '推导 3 个优先拓扑的 ASV 表达式。形式化证明 monotonicity 和 sharpness。\n\n    MC 验证：coverage at 90%, 95%, 99% across 1000 scenarios/topology。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    monotonicity_proved:\n    - confounding\n    - mediation\n    - collider\n    sharpness_proved:\n    - confounding\n    - mediation\n    sharpness_incomplete:\n    - collider\n    sharpness_formal_proofs_count: 2\n    collider_sharpness_numerical: achieving 93% of bound in 10k optimization runs\n    coverage_at_95_nominal:\n      confounding: 0.93\n      mediation: 0.9\n      collider: 0.91\n    coverage_at_90_nominal:\n      confounding: 0.95\n      mediation: 0.92\n      collider: 0.93\n    coverage_at_99_nominal:\n      confounding: 0.97\n      mediation: 0.96\n      collider: 0.95\n    average_coverage_95: 0.913\n  result_rationale: 'Monotonicity 对所有 3 个拓扑成立（proved）因为：更大的 δ 意味着 sensitivity set\n    中考虑更极端的 C →\n\n    overturn conclusion 所需的 minimum perturbation 只能增加或不变。\n\n    这与 underlying bias 是否单调无关——ASV 是 min-over-C 量，不是 pointwise bias。\n\n\n    Confounding sharpness：bias 在 C 的 off-diagonal elements 上是线性的，supremum 有 clean\n    convex structure，\n\n    sharpness-achieving C 在 feasible set 的顶点。构造性证明。\n\n\n    Mediation sharpness：尽管存在方向反转，ASV sharpness 仍可证——通过分别分析 attenuation regime 和 reversal\n    regime。\n\n    Reversal boundary 处的 worst-case C 恰好达到 bound——构造性证明利用 phase transition 结构。\n\n    这是一个 nice 的结果：有反转的拓扑仍然有 tight bound，加强了 ASV 框架的可信度。\n\n\n    Collider sharpness INCOMPLETE：bias 表达式涉及 conditioning on misclassified Z，\n\n    产生 E[Y|X,Z*] = Σ_z P(Z=z|Z*) E[Y|X,Z=z]。\n\n    对 C 做 supremum 要求联合优化 P(Z=z|Z*)，subject to C 为 valid confusion matrix，\n\n    产生非凸 bilinear 约束。数值优化达到 analytical bound 的 93%，强烈暗示 sharpness，\n\n    但形式化证明 supremum is attained 被 feasible set 的非凸拓扑阻断。\n\n\n    Coverage 略低于 nominal（average 91.3% at 95% nominal）因为 ASV bounds 在已知 exact C 下推导，\n\n    而 MC 用的是有限样本估计的 C。Gap（3.7%）反映估计不确定性而非 bound failure。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: ASV Proof Status and Coverage (Priority Topologies)\n    columns:\n    - topology\n    - monotonicity\n    - sharpness\n    - coverage_90\n    - coverage_95\n    - coverage_99\n    rows:\n    - - confounding\n      - formal proof\n      - formal proof\n      - 0.95\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.97\n    - - mediation\n      - formal proof\n      - formal proof\n      - 0.92\n      - 0.9\n      - 0.96\n    - - collider\n      - formal proof\n      - numerical only (93%)\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.95\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 13: ASV curves — ASV vs δ for 3 topologies，with MC pointwise confidence bands。Monotonicity\n    直观可见。Mediation 曲线斜率更陡（对 amplification 更敏感）。'\n  - 'Fig 14: Coverage calibration plots — nominal level (x) vs empirical coverage\n    (y)。全部略低于对角线（mildly anti-conservative），confounding 最接近校准。'\n  - 'Fig 15: Sharpness illustration — confounding + mediation 展示 achieving C matrix\n    + bound value；collider 展示 best numerical C 与 analytical bound 的 gap。'\n  analysis: 'ASV 框架在 3 个优先拓扑上验证：monotonicity universally proved，sharpness 2/3 proved。\n\n    Collider sharpness gap（7%）是主要技术障碍——论文应增加一段讨论 conditioning-on-misclassified-variable\n    导致的非凸优化问题，\n\n    并标记 convex relaxation approach 为 future work。\n\n    Mediation 的更陡 ASV 曲线意味着 mediation DAGs 的结论对 annotation error 更敏感——\n\n    与 direction reversal 发现一致，自然连接 Claim 1 和 Claim 2。\n\n    '\n- name: ASV MC Validation for M-bias, Instrument, Front-door\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: '推导剩余 3 个拓扑的 ASV 表达式 + MC 验证。\n\n    Monotonicity 和 coverage 验证。Sharpness 作为 conjectures + numerical evidence。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    monotonicity_holds:\n    - M-bias\n    - instrument\n    - front-door\n    monotonicity_failures: 0\n    sharpness_numerical:\n      mbias: achieving 92% of bound\n      instrument: achieving 89% of bound\n      frontdoor: achieving 94% of bound\n    coverage_at_95_nominal:\n      mbias: 0.9\n      instrument: 0.89\n      frontdoor: 0.91\n    instrument_conservatism: ASV bounds 1.8× wider than necessary\n    total_asv_coverage_6_topologies: 0.907\n  result_rationale: 'Monotonicity 对所有 3 个拓扑成立——与 plan_004 相同的结构性论证：\n\n    ASV 是 minimum-over-perturbation 量，在 perturbation budget δ 中固有单调。\n\n\n    Sharpness numerical evidence 有差异：front-door 最接近 tight（94%，identification structure\n    较简单），\n\n    M-bias 中等（92%），instrument 最远（89%）。\n\n    Instrument gap 反映 Wald estimator 的 ratio structure——supremum 涉及优化 misclassified\n    量的 ratio，\n\n    landscape 有多个 local optima。\n\n\n    Instrument ASV 显著保守（1.8× wider）因为 Wald estimator 放大小分母扰动，\n\n    worst-case bound 比 typical case 差很多。这是 IV sensitivity analysis 的已知问题（非本框架特有）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: ASV Results for Secondary Topologies\n    columns:\n    - topology\n    - monotonicity\n    - sharpness_numerical_pct\n    - coverage_95\n    - conservatism\n    rows:\n    - - M-bias\n      - holds\n      - 92%\n      - 0.9\n      - comparable to collider\n    - - instrument\n      - holds\n      - 89%\n      - 0.89\n      - 1.8× conservative (Wald ratio)\n    - - front-door\n      - holds\n      - 94%\n      - 0.91\n      - near-tight\n  - name: All 6 Topologies ASV Summary\n    columns:\n    - topology\n    - monotonicity\n    - sharpness_status\n    - coverage_95\n    rows:\n    - - confounding\n      - proved\n      - proved (formal)\n      - 0.93\n    - - mediation\n      - proved\n      - proved (formal)\n      - 0.9\n    - - collider\n      - proved\n      - 93% numerical\n      - 0.91\n    - - M-bias\n      - proved\n      - 92% numerical\n      - 0.9\n    - - instrument\n      - proved\n      - 89% numerical\n      - 0.89\n    - - front-door\n      - proved\n      - 94% numerical\n      - 0.91\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 16: ASV curves for secondary topologies — same format as Fig 13。Instrument\n    曲线显著更宽（更保守）。'\n  - 'Fig 17: Sharpness gap comparison — 6 topologies bar chart of (1 − numerical_achievement/bound)。Confounding\n    + mediation at 0% (proved)，others at 6–11%。'\n  analysis: '6 个拓扑全部有 ASV 表达式 + validated monotonicity。Sharpness landscape：\n\n    2 proved (confounding, mediation) + 4 numerical (collider 93%, front-door 94%,\n    M-bias 92%, instrument 89%)。\n\n    Instrument 是最弱环节——ASV 保守性限制了实用性。论文应诚实讨论并标记 tighter instrument-specific bounds\n    为 future work。\n\n    Overall average 95%-nominal coverage = 0.907，在 median 档 [0.88, 0.93] 范围内。\n\n    '\n- name: ASV Calibration on Empirical Data\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '将 ASVs 应用于 plan_003 的经验 confusion matrices，跨 3 CSS tasks × 3 LLMs。\n\n    在 held-out gold-standard splits 上验证 coverage。\n\n    比较 ASV 可解释性与 raw confusion matrix reporting。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_scenarios: 9\n    empirical_asv_concordance: 7\n    concordance_failures: 2\n    failure_scenarios:\n    - toxicity-Llama4 vs toxicity-Qwen35\n    - toxicity-Qwen35 vs toxicity-DeepSeek\n    failure_reason: all 3 models produce high ASVs (>2.0) for toxicity K=2; differences\n      within estimation noise\n    asv_ranking:\n      protest: DeepSeek (0.91) > Llama4 (0.82) > Qwen35 (0.68) — correct\n      stance: DeepSeek (1.41) > Llama4 (1.24) > Qwen35 (1.08) — correct\n      toxicity: DeepSeek (2.44) ≈ Llama4 (2.31) ≈ Qwen35 (2.18) — indistinguishable\n    held_out_coverage_95: 0.89\n  result_rationale: 'Concordance 7/9：ASV 在 protest (K=5) 和 stance (K=3) 任务上正确排序模型鲁棒性——\n\n    这些任务的 confusion matrix 差异足够大，产生有区分力的 ASV 值。\n\n    Failure 出现在 toxicity (K=2)：所有 3 个模型有 near-diagonal C（accuracy > 0.86），\n\n    产生高 ASVs (>2.0)，差异在 MC estimation noise 内——无法区分模型。\n\n\n    这是 low-bias regime 的结构性限制：annotation quality 高时（K=2 toxicity），\n\n    ASVs 正确指示\"robust\"但不能 rank-order models。\n\n    这实际上是合适的——如果所有模型产生 negligible bias，ranking 本身就无信息量。\n\n\n    Held-out coverage (0.89 at 95% nominal) 略低于 MC coverage (0.91) 因为 empirical C\n    有额外的\n\n    gold-standard sample size 估计噪声。Gap 小且在预期范围内。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: ASV Values and Concordance by Task × Model\n    columns:\n    - task\n    - model\n    - ASV_95\n    - observed_abs_bias\n    - robust_flag\n    - concordant\n    rows:\n    - - protest\n      - Llama 4\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.09\n      - moderate\n      - true\n    - - protest\n      - Qwen 3.5\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.12\n      - fragile\n      - true\n    - - protest\n      - DeepSeek\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.05\n      - moderate-high\n      - true\n    - - stance\n      - Llama 4\n      - 1.24\n      - 0.06\n      - moderate-high\n      - true\n    - - stance\n      - Qwen 3.5\n      - 1.08\n      - 0.08\n      - moderate\n      - true\n    - - stance\n      - DeepSeek\n      - 1.41\n      - 0.03\n      - high\n      - true\n    - - toxicity\n      - Llama 4\n      - 2.31\n      - 0.02\n      - high\n      - true\n    - - toxicity\n      - Qwen 3.5\n      - 2.18\n      - 0.04\n      - high\n      - false\n    - - toxicity\n      - DeepSeek\n      - 2.44\n      - 0.01\n      - high\n      - false\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 18: ASV vs observed absolute bias scatter — 9 scenarios。Protest + stance\n    展示 negative correlation；toxicity 聚集在右上角（high ASV, low bias, indistinguishable）。'\n  - 'Fig 19: ASV vs raw C matrix comparison — side-by-side 对比 2 个 example scenarios，展示\n    ASV 提供 single interpretable number vs 9–25 cell matrix。'\n  analysis: 'ASVs 在 moderate-to-high bias scenarios 中具有经验实用性（protest K=5, stance K=3），\n\n    但在 low-bias regime 失去区分力（toxicity K=2）。这是诚实且预期的——\n\n    类似 E-values 在 confounding 小时不 informative。\n\n    论文应 frame 为：\"ASVs are most valuable when annotation error is non-trivial (K≥3,\n    accuracy <0.85)——\n\n    precisely the scenarios where researchers lack existing diagnostic tools。\"\n\n    7/9 concordance 支持 Claim 2 的实用价值。\n\n    '\n- name: 'Correction Guidance Framework: Decision Mapping and Validation'\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'Decision framework: {topology × error structure × ASV} → correction\n    method\n\n    (DSL / PPI / MLA / naive plug-in / \"no existing method adequate\")。\n\n    MC validation: 90 scenarios + empirical validation on plan_003 data。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_mc_scenarios: 90\n    correction_framework_accuracy: 0.89\n    correct_recommendations: 80\n    boundary_indistinguishable_cases: 3\n    hard_failure_cases: 7\n    failure_breakdown:\n      near_diagonal_all_methods_equivalent: 3\n      differential_intermediate_mismatch: 2\n      false_recommendation_in_hopeless_regime: 2\n    method_dominance:\n      DSL: best in 28/90 (diagonal-dominant C, confounding/mediation)\n      PPI: best in 22/90 (moderate C, exposure/front-door)\n      MLA: best in 18/90 (high off-diagonal, confounding/collider)\n      naive_plugin: best in 12/90 (near-diagonal, any topology)\n      no_method_adequate: 10/90 (near-permutation + reversal topologies)\n    empirical_validation_plan003:\n      protest_correct: true\n      stance_correct: true\n      toxicity_correct: true\n    open_problems:\n    - dependence-aware multi-LLM correction\n    - differential K≥3 error correction\n    - collider + near-permutation C (no method reduces bias below 50%)\n  result_rationale: '89% accuracy 反映框架在 clear-cut scenarios（方法性能明显分离）的优势和 boundary\n    cases 的弱点。\n\n\n    3 个 boundary cases 是结构性不可区分的：near-diagonal C（low error）下所有方法结果相近（within 5%），\n\n    \"best\" recommendation 是任意的。这不是框架的失败而是问题本身的 degeneracy。\n\n\n    7 个 hard failures：\n\n    (a) 3 cases: near-diagonal C 使所有方法等效但框架因 threshold effects 选了次优方法；\n\n    (b) 2 cases: intermediate differential error 处框架的 non-differential/differential\n    二分类\n\n    无法捕获 differentiality 的连续性质；\n\n    (c) 2 cases: 框架推荐了方法但正确答案是\"no method adequate\"（near-permutation C + reversal topology）。\n\n\n    Method dominance 是 topology-driven 的：DSL 擅长 confounding（调整 misclassified confounder\n    是其 native use case），\n\n    PPI 擅长 exposure（regression-calibration 处理 treatment misclassification），\n\n    MLA 擅长 high off-diagonal error（maximum likelihood 直接建模 C）。\n\n\n    10/90 \"no method adequate\" 集中在 reversal topologies（exposure, mediation）+ extreme\n    C——\n\n    这些是 current correction literature 的真实 gaps。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Correction Method Dominance Map\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - best_in_n\n    - primary_topology\n    - primary_error_regime\n    rows:\n    - - DSL\n      - 28\n      - confounding, mediation\n      - diagonal-dominant C\n    - - PPI\n      - 22\n      - exposure, front-door\n      - moderate off-diagonal\n    - - MLA\n      - 18\n      - confounding, collider\n      - high off-diagonal\n    - - naive plug-in\n      - 12\n      - any\n      - near-diagonal\n    - - no method\n      - 10\n      - exposure, mediation\n      - near-permutation\n  - name: Framework Failure Analysis\n    columns:\n    - failure_type\n    - count\n    - impact\n    - mitigation\n    rows:\n    - - boundary (methods ≤5% apart)\n      - 3\n      - low\n      - any recommendation acceptable\n    - - differential mismatch\n      - 2\n      - moderate\n      - add continuous differentiality parameter\n    - - false recommendation in hopeless regime\n      - 2\n      - high\n      - 'add safety check: if reversal topology + extreme C → flag'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 20: Decision tree / flowchart — {topology, error structure, ASV} → recommended\n    method。Color-coded by method，boundary regions highlighted。'\n  - 'Fig 21: Method accuracy heatmap — topology (rows) × error structure bins (cols)\n    → recommendation accuracy。Diagonal patterns showing topology-method alignment。'\n  - 'Fig 22: Open problems map — (off-diagonal mass, differentiality) 2D scatter colored\n    by adequate method existence。Gap region in upper-right clearly visible。'\n  analysis: 'Correction framework 达到主要目标：89% 正确识别 best correction method。\n\n    11% failure rate 集中在固有歧义的 boundary cases（3%）和真正困难的 regimes（8%）。\n\n    2 个\"false recommendation in hopeless regime\"最令人担忧——框架提供了虚假信心。\n\n    论文应明确讨论此风险并建议 practitioners 始终在 held-out data 上验证 corrections。\n\n    10 个\"no method adequate\"scenarios 是论文对 open problems 的贡献——\n\n    特别是 dependence-aware multi-LLM correction（结合 plan_003 的 correlation 发现）。\n\n    '\n- name: Pathological Confusion Matrix Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: '极端 C 结构分析：near-permutation, rank-deficient, block-diagonal。\n\n    刻画 catastrophic bias 条件并识别结构性预测因子。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    spectral_gap_predictive_R2: 0.78\n    diagonal_dominance_predictive_R2: 0.71\n    combined_predictor_R2: 0.84\n    catastrophic_threshold_spectral_gap: 0.3\n    catastrophic_threshold_diagonal_dominance: 0.5\n    near_permutation_universally_catastrophic: true\n    rank_deficient_topology_dependent: true\n    rank_deficient_worst:\n    - front-door\n    - instrument\n    block_diagonal_worst: mediation (blocks indirect path)\n  result_rationale: 'Spectral gap（C 的第一和第二 eigenvalue 之差）预测 bias severity（R²=0.78）\n\n    因为它捕获了 C 距 permutation matrix 的距离——反转的结构性来源。\n\n    R²=0.78 表示强但不完美的预测；剩余方差来自 topology-specific interactions。\n\n\n    Diagonal dominance（minimum diagonal element）是更简单的 proxy，R² 略低（0.71）。\n\n    Combined spectral gap + diagonal dominance 达到 R²=0.84——两个 features 捕获了大部分 bias-relevant\n    C structure。\n\n\n    Near-permutation 普遍 catastrophic 因为 label-swapping 搅乱所有拓扑。\n\n    Rank-deficient C 是 topology-dependent：front-door 和 instrument 的 identification\n    formula\n\n    含有 C-dependent 分母——C rank-deficient 时分母趋零，bias unbounded。\n\n    Confounding/mediation/collider 对 rank deficiency 处理更 graceful（无 ratio estimator）。\n\n\n    Block-diagonal C 对 mediation 最 severe——block 结构可以创造 artifact category boundaries\n    上的 apparent indirect effects。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Structural Predictors of Bias Severity\n    columns:\n    - predictor\n    - R2_overall\n    - best_topology_R2\n    - worst_topology_R2\n    rows:\n    - - spectral gap\n      - 0.78\n      - exposure (0.85)\n      - M-bias (0.67)\n    - - diagonal dominance\n      - 0.71\n      - confounding (0.82)\n      - front-door (0.58)\n    - - spectral gap + diag dom\n      - 0.84\n      - exposure (0.91)\n      - instrument (0.74)\n  - name: Catastrophic Bias Conditions by Topology and C Structure\n    columns:\n    - topology\n    - near_permutation\n    - rank_deficient\n    - block_diagonal\n    rows:\n    - - confounding\n      - severe (OVB > 2×)\n      - moderate\n      - moderate\n    - - exposure\n      - catastrophic (reversal)\n      - severe\n      - severe (block reversal)\n    - - mediation\n      - severe (reversal)\n      - moderate\n      - severe (block indirect effects)\n    - - collider\n      - severe (attenuation > 60%)\n      - moderate\n      - moderate\n    - - M-bias\n      - moderate\n      - moderate\n      - mild\n    - - instrument\n      - moderate\n      - catastrophic (Wald denom → 0)\n      - moderate\n    - - front-door\n      - moderate\n      - catastrophic (identification loss)\n      - moderate\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 23: Spectral gap vs bias severity scatter — one panel/topology，threshold\n    at 0.3 where bias becomes catastrophic。'\n  - 'Fig 24: Phase diagram — spectral gap (x) × diagonal dominance (y) → bias regime\n    (safe/moderate/catastrophic)。Sharp boundaries visible。'\n  - 'Fig 25: Rank deficiency impact — bias magnitude vs effective matrix rank for\n    each topology。Front-door + instrument 在 rank 降低时 diverge。'\n  analysis: '实用 takeaway：spectral gap < 0.3 OR diagonal dominance < 0.5 → 所有拓扑均高风险。\n\n    这一双阈值规则足够简单可用且捕获 84% 的 bias variance。\n\n    Front-door 和 instrument 对 rank-deficient C 特别脆弱（ratio estimator 分母问题）。\n\n    这些 structural predictors 是 toolkit (plan_010) 的 automatic diagnostic features\n    候选。\n\n    '\n- name: annot-sensitivity Python Toolkit\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 'Open-source pip-installable package：user-specified DAG + confusion\n    matrix + downstream estimate\n\n    → bias expressions + ASV + sensitivity curves + correction recommendation + diagnostic\n    plots。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    package_name: annot-sensitivity\n    supported_topologies: 6\n    supported_K_range: 2–10\n    core_api:\n    - compute_bias(dag, C, estimate) → BiasResult\n    - compute_asv(dag, C, estimate, delta_range) → ASVResult\n    - recommend_correction(dag, C, asv) → CorrectionRecommendation\n    - diagnostic_plot(result) → Figure\n    - eigendecomp_summary(C, K) → EigenSummary\n    - check_pathological(C) → PathologyReport (spectral gap + diag dom thresholds)\n    worked_examples: 3\n    example_topologies:\n    - confounding (baseline)\n    - exposure (reversal)\n    - mediation (conditional reversal)\n    test_coverage: 0.87\n    documentation: API reference + 3 tutorial notebooks + quick-start guide\n    known_limitations:\n    - K>7 eigendecomposition slow (>10s/computation)\n    - correction accuracy inherits plan_007 limitations (89%)\n    - CLI + notebook only, no GUI\n    - 3/6 topologies lack detailed tutorials (M-bias, instrument, front-door)\n  result_rationale: '3 个 worked examples（而非 6）因为 median 档 scope 有限——优先覆盖 3 个 reversal-relevant\n    拓扑\n\n    （confounding 作为 baseline，exposure + mediation 作为反转案例）。剩余 3 个拓扑在 API 中支持但缺少详细 tutorial。\n\n\n    K>7 性能限制反映 eigendecomposition 的 O(K³) 成本——对典型 CSS 使用（K=3–7）可接受，\n\n    对罕见 high-K 应用偏慢。\n\n\n    Test coverage 0.87 反映核心计算（bias expressions, ASV）的 thorough unit testing\n\n    和 visualization/correction recommendation 组件的 lighter testing。\n\n\n    check_pathological() 集成 plan_009 的 spectral gap + diagonal dominance 阈值，\n\n    为 practitioner 提供自动 C matrix 质量诊断。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 26 (toolkit demo): Notebook screenshot — exposure DAG K=3 的完整输出：bias expression,\n    ASV curve, correction recommendation, diagnostic plot，in a single cell。'\n  analysis: 'Toolkit 是 functional deliverable，使论文的理论贡献对 practitioners 可及。\n\n    3 个 worked examples 覆盖最重要的场景（reversal cases）。\n\n    主要 gap：3 个拓扑缺少 tutorial，可能限制 M-bias/instrument/front-door 用户的采纳。\n\n    Post-publication 低成本 follow-up。'\n","numLines":1449,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1449}}}
