{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Ad6difmAP2BnXucxwJz2NF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper and the review context YAML. Let me now dispatch the two reviewers in parallel:\n\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nI'll use two agents running in parallel for the independent review step (Step 1), then proceed through the roundtable steps.\n\nLet me carefully structure the review. The paper is:\n\n**Title:** \"Multi-Class Annotation Errors Are Not Created Equal: Bias Taxonomy, Sensitivity Analysis, and Correction Guidance for LLM-Annotated Causal Studies\"\n\n**Summary:** The paper develops a framework for analyzing multi-class annotation error propagation in causal inference across 6 DAG topologies. \n\nThe core contributions are a taxonomy showing how direction reversal varies by topology, a formal sensitivity analysis framework with Annotation Sensitivity Values, and practical correction guidance, all validated across three causal inference tasks using three different LLMs.\n\nNow I'm launching both reviewers as parallel agents.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14170,"cache_read_input_tokens":44364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14170},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44efd5d7-3d5f-464d-80ca-d3c01b5a58d8","uuid":"f3fa8eb1-4765-43aa-b6a0-9fadf99a7a4d"}
